00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:39.490
And when I was a producer in season nine, I got to stay for the notes sessions.
而且当我在第九季担任制片人时，我有机会留下来参加意见反馈会。

158
00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.990
And they were fascinating.
而且它们非常引人入胜。

159
00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:43.470
Fascinating.
太吸引人了。

160
00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:51.210
Sometimes it would just be as small as like, hey, I want you to write alt jokes for that line.
有时可能只是微不足道的小事，比如，嘿，我想让你为那句台词写几个备选笑话。

161
00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:56.550
And then sometimes it would be whole storylines that they would say, I think we need to rethink this.
有时则是整条故事线，他们会说，我觉得我们需要重新考虑这个。

162
00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.230
We need to reinvent this.
我们需要重新构思这个。

163
00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.930
It needs more conflict or it needs more something fascinating.
它需要更多的冲突，或者需要更多吸引人的东西。

164
00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:06.290
And as far as the final table read, that was really a huge deal.
至于最后的剧本围读，那真的是一件大事。

165
00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.270
We weren't in our writer's trailer because we were on location.
我们不在编剧的拖车里，因为我们在外景地。

166
00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.970
So we were in this big room.
所以我们在一个很大的房间里。

167
00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:19.670
There were rows and rows and rows of chairs for anyone that had ever worked on the show in any way, was there and was watching.
有一排又一排的椅子，任何曾经以某种方式参与过这部剧的人都在那里观看。

168
00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:21.950
They had a camera set up to film it.
他们架设了摄像机来拍摄。

169
00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.270
Yeah, we did not usually film our table reads.
对，我们通常不拍摄剧本围读。

170
00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:28.550
And there was, you know, Chris Haston took photos.
而且，你知道的，克里斯·哈斯顿拍了照片。

171
00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.590
But several people took pictures.
但有好几个人都在拍照。

172
00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.950
Like just even from our crew, people were just documenting the moment.
甚至我们的剧组成员，大家都在记录这个时刻。

173
00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:34.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

174
00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:38.250
And the table was set up in this huge like U shape.
桌子摆成了一个巨大的U形。

175
00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:38.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

176
00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.150
And we had microphones, which we normally didn't have.
我们还有麦克风，平时我们是没有的。

177
00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:51.490
Yeah, and we would have the occasional NBC executive stop by our weekly table reads, but we were far from the main lot.
对，偶尔会有NBC的高管顺道来参加我们每周的剧本围读，但我们离主片场很远。

178
00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.110
And they did not make that track.
他们不会特意跑那一趟。

179
00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:59.110
But for the final table read, it was like every executive who worked at NBC was at that table read.
但对于最后的剧本围读，感觉所有在NBC工作的执行高管都出席了。

180
00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.790
It was a huge deal.
这可是一件大事。

181
00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:01.530
Huge deal.
超级大事。

182
00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:11.410
And our table reads for so many years, like Jenna said, I mean, the first year we sat in a circle on the stage, like the Dunder Mifflin office.
而且多年来我们的剧本围读，就像珍娜说的，第一年我们围坐在舞台上，就像邓德米夫林的办公室一样。

183
00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:15.690
Yeah, we just pulled our rolly chairs up around the Dwight Gym desk clump.
对，我们只是把带轮子的椅子拉到德怀特吉姆的办公桌堆旁边。

184
00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.190
Yeah, and we would just sit there.
对，我们就坐在那儿。

185
00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:22.070
In fact, when my parents visited in the early seasons of the office, we did the table read.
事实上，在我父母在《办公室》早期几季来探班时，我们正好在进行剧本围读。

186
00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:28.470
And my parents sat in a rolly chair by like Creed's desk and listened to us read the script.
我父母坐在克里德的办公桌旁边的转椅上，听我们读剧本。

187
00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.510
So it was kind of interesting to see the progression.
所以看到这种演变过程挺有意思的。

188
00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:36.990
And then as the years went on, then we had the trailer and then we had network execs that would come.
后来随着时间的推移，我们有了拖车，然后开始有电视网高管过来。

189
00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.610
And then, yeah, ended it with this huge crowd.
然后，是的，以这样庞大的观众群结束。

190
00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.270
Yeah.
对。

191
00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:42.930
All right.
好了。

192
00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:43.830
Well, that was fun.
嗯，这挺有意思的。

193
00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:44.530
Yeah.
对。

194
00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.950
Thank you so much for that question.
非常感谢你提出这个问题。

195
00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:49.530
I actually just loved revisiting all of that in my brain.
我其实很喜欢在脑海中重新温习这一切。

196
00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:50.690
It was fun to remember.
回忆起来很有趣。

197
00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:51.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

198
00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:52.070
All right.
好了。

199
00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.390
Well, listen, why don't we take a break?
那么，听着，我们为什么不休息一下呢？

200
00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:56.390
And when we come back, I'm going to share about Lake of the Ozarks.
等我们回来后，我要分享关于奥沙克湖的事。

201
00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.690
Where I want to go with you.
我想和你一起去的地方。

202
00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.250
I want to go with you.
我想跟你一起去。

203
00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.190
I need to go.
我得走了。

204
00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.550
And I can't wait to hear about your trip.
我迫不及待想听你讲讲你的旅行。

205
00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:12.710
All right.
好吧。

206
00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:13.730
We are back from break.
我们休息回来了。

207
00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:18.170
And are you ready to go to the Lake of the Ozarks with Jenna Fisher?
你们准备好和珍娜·费舍尔一起去奥沙克湖了吗？

208
00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.170
All right.
好的。

209
00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:22.130
Well, here we go.
好了，我们开始吧。

210
00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.910
I journaled each morning just to give you some context.
我每天早上都会写日记，好给你们提供一些背景。

211
00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:31.930
I was going to ask you about that because I would jot things down as my day went in my notes app.
我本来想问你这个，因为我平时都是把事情随手记在手机便签里的。

212
00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:32.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

213
00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:36.110
And then I would either have to journal like at night or in the morning the next day.
然后我要么得在晚上，要么得在第二天早上补写日记。

214
00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:36.550
Yes.
对。

215
00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:40.270
Because it was, you know, wall-to-wall activities all day, family, all that.
因为你知道的，整整一天排满了各种活动，还要陪家人，诸如此类。

216
00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.490
So here we go.
所以我们开始吧。

217
00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:44.330
Lake of the Ozarks summer travel journal.
奥沙克湖夏季旅行日记。

218
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.450
First morning at the lake.
在湖边的第一个早晨。

219
00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:48.630
You're sitting so properly.
你坐得太端正了。

220
00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:49.730
I wish you guys could see her.
我真希望你们能看到她的样子。

221
00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.850
She's like with her hands clasped in front of her.
她双手交叠在身前。

222
00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:53.650
I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

223
00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.150
I feel like I'm giving a speech.
我觉得自己好像在发表演讲。

224
00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:55.530
Okay.
好啦。

225
00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:58.510
I'm sitting out under a big covered patio.
我坐在一个巨大的带顶露台下面。

226
00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:02.950
It has two ceiling fans, which is amazing because we were having a heat wave.
这里有两个吊扇，太棒了，因为我们正赶上热浪。

227
00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:04.930
It's 940 a.m.
现在是上午9点40分。

228
00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.970
and it's already 90 degrees outside.
外面已经华氏90度了。

229
00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:07.450
Whew.
哇。

230
00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.690
We are here during the week before 4th of July.
我们是在独立日前的一周来到这里的。

231
00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:16.910
I hope that means the lake will be less busy and we can go for a long boat ride without getting thrown around too much.
我希望这意味着湖上人会少一点，我们可以痛痛快快地开着快艇兜风，而不会被颠得太厉害。

232
00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:20.630
My folks have had a place at Lake of the Ozarks since I was 8 years old.
我爸妈自我8岁起就在奥沙克湖有栋房产。

233
00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.310
Or maybe my sister was 8 and I was 13.
或者也许那时我妹8岁，我13岁。

234
00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.610
I'll have to ask my mom.
我得去问问我妈。

235
00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.850
But we came here even before that.
但在此之前我们就已经来过这里了。

236
00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.650
Every summer from as far back as I can recall.
从我有记忆以来的每个夏天都是如此。

237
00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:34.110
I think it's safe to say I've been coming here for over 45 years.
我想我可以肯定地说，我来这里已经超过45年了。

238
00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:37.030
Older than some of y'all listening.
比听节目的某些人年纪还要大。

239
00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:37.610
Yes.
是的。

240
00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:42.630
Thank you for making that clear.
谢谢你把这一点挑明。

241
00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:52.510
My parents' place started as a two-bedroom cabin they had built on a spot that I remember first visiting by boat.
我父母的房子最初是一个两居室的小屋，是他们在当年我记得第一次乘船来访的地方建的。

242
00:10:52.510 --> 00:11:03.550
It is in a quiet side cove and there is a soft rocky beach and I remember pulling our little red speedboat up onto that shore, tying it to a tree with a long yellow plasticky rope,
它在一个安静的小海湾里，有一片卵石和细沙交织的柔缓海滩，我记得当时我们把我们那艘红色小快艇开上岸，用一根长长的黄色塑料绳把它拴在树上，

243
00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:07.790
having a picnic lunch, and watching my parents talk about putting a house there.
吃着野餐，看着我父母商量着要在那里建一栋房子。

244
00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.370
The soft rocky beach was discussed many times as a big plus.
那片柔缓的沙滩曾被反复讨论，被认为是一个巨大的优势。

245
00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:17.870
It meant we could slowly wade into the water from shore while we waited for a dock to be built.
这意味着在等待码头建好的那段时间里，我们可以从岸边慢慢涉水走到水里。

246
00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.070
Had they already bought the land?
他们当时已经买下那块地了吗？

247
00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.150
I'm not sure.
我不确定。

248
00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.770
Again, maybe I should ask about these details.
话说回来，也许我该去问问这些细节。

249
00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:28.150
But more than anything, I think it's cool that they made this dream come true for themselves.
但最重要的是，我觉得他们能为自己实现这个梦想真的很酷。

250
00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:32.110
I remember driving down over the next year watching as the house was built.
我记得第二年开车南下的时候，眼睁睁地看着那栋房子一点点建起来。

251
00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.630
All of the anticipatory excitement.
所有的期待与兴奋。

252
00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:45.170
Two bedrooms, one bath, a utility room, which also houses the washer dryer and all of my dad's tools, a kitchen living room, and a great big deck facing the lake.
两间卧室、一间浴室、一间兼作洗衣机烘干机房以及放我爸所有工具的杂物间、一个起居室兼厨房，还有一个正对湖面的超大露台。

253
00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:53.090
I remember their decision to put their bedroom in the front of the house with a lake view and deck access and our bedroom in the back of the house.
我记得他们决定把自己的卧室放在前面，带有湖景和露台出入口，而我们的卧室则在房子后面。

254
00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:57.090
Theirs was small, just big enough for a queen bed and two nightstands.
他们的很小，刚好能放下一张双人床和两个床头柜。

255
00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:05.610
Ours was much bigger with bunk beds and a couch and a large walk-in closet, which served as a place to put life vests, overflow food items, skis,
我们的要大得多，有双层床、一张沙发和一个大型步入式衣帽间，里面放着救生衣、囤积的食物、滑雪板，

256
00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.630
and even a drying rack for swimsuits.
甚至还有一个晾泳衣的架子。

257
00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:08.830
That's a big closet.
那可真是个大衣帽间。

258
00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.250
It was really big.
真的很大。

259
00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:12.950
You could almost fit a twin bed in there.
你甚至能在里面塞下一张单人床。

260
00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.590
It was almost like another room.
它简直就像另一个房间。

261
00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:19.230
When we were teenagers, we could put blankets on the ground and hide in the closet for privacy.
当我们是青少年时，我们可以在地上铺上毯子，躲在衣帽间里寻求隐私。

262
00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.710
Incidentally, the bunk beds had no railing on the upper bunk.
顺便说一句，双层床的上铺是没有护栏的。

263
00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.490
It's not like how they are today.
不像现在的那些。

264
00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:29.530
And since I was older, I got the top bunk, even though my daredevil sister really wanted it.
而且因为我比较大，我睡上铺，尽管我那个喜欢冒险的妹妹其实很想要它。

265
00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:33.430
I fell out of that bed in the middle of the night at least once a year.
我每年至少有一次在半夜从那张床上摔下来。

266
00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:41.250
I do feel like our generation was just like, well, just fear it out.
我确实觉得我们那代人的态度就是，好吧，自己克服恐惧吧。

267
00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:42.990
No spells.
没有防护。

268
00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.690
Yeah, you'll be fine.
行吧，你会没事的。

269
00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:47.410
And you can lay on the floorboard while we drive.
我们开车时你还可以躺在车厢地板上。

270
00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.610
The top bunk now belongs to my niece.
现在的上铺属于我侄女了。

271
00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.270
And we laughed about the fact that she, too, has fallen out in the middle of the night.
我们还笑着谈论这样一个事实：她也在半夜摔下来过。

272
00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:58.230
My dad even attempted to add a safety railing, but I guess it didn't work.
我爸甚至尝试加装一个安全护栏，但我想没起作用。

273
00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.710
So the bed is still...
所以那张床依然……

274
00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.190
The bunk bed is still there from my childhood.
那张自我童年起就在的双层床还在那儿。

275
00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.130
It's still taking victims today?
它现在还在收割受害者吗？

276
00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.250
With no railing.
而且还没有护栏。

277
00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:12.330
Well, my sister was like, if my children are going to sleep in this bunk bed, Dad, it needs some sort of railing.
嗯，我妹妹当时说，爸，如果我的孩子要睡这张双层床，它得有个什么护栏才行。

278
00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:15.890
But then my niece and I were talking and she was like, oh, yeah, I saw a lot of that.
但后来我和我侄女聊天时，她说，哦，对啊，我经常经历那种情况。

279
00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:16.630
Like, let's see.
比如，让我想想。

280
00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.130
She just went right through the railing?
她直接穿过了那个护栏？

281
00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.350
Yeah, I guess so.
对，我猜是的。

282
00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.870
And I was like, oh, no, CeCe.
然后我说，哦，不，西西。

283
00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:22.590
We bonded.
我们因此建立起了感情。

284
00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:23.570
Moving on.
言归正传。

285
00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.110
I'm almost done with morning one.
我快要把第一天上午的部分讲完了。

286
00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:31.170
A few years ago, my parents expanded the house, adding on a second story and two additional bedrooMs.
几年前，我父母扩建了房子，加盖了第二层和另外两间卧室。

287
00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:38.790
It's big enough now that my sister and her kids can come down and stay, but not quite big enough to also house me and Lee and our kids.
现在它足够大了，我妹妹和她的孩子们可以过来住，但还不足以同时容纳我和李以及我们的孩子。

288
00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.550
So we usually get an Airbnb somewhere nearby.
所以我们通常会在附近租个爱彼迎。

289
00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:44.290
Our place this year is great.
我们今年住的地方很棒。

290
00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.010
I slept so well in the bedroom.
我在那个卧室里睡得太好了。

291
00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.950
That was in all caps, so well.
那可是全大写的“太好了”。

292
00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:55.610
Now, this is the one thing you shared with me about this trip because we tried to keep secrets so that we could share them today.
话说明白了，这是你关于这次旅行唯一跟我分享的事，因为我们试图保守秘密，好在今天分享出来。

293
00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.130
But you were like, oh, my God, ladies.
但你当时说，哦，天哪，女士们。

294
00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:00.250
I slept so well.
我睡得太好了。

295
00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:03.390
To know Jenna is to know how important sleep is.
认识珍娜的人都知道睡眠有多重要。

296
00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.430
Yeah, it's true.
是的，没错。

297
00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.790
I wrote, great mattress.
我写了，床垫很棒。

298
00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:13.590
But the best thing is the big covered deck with the fans facing the lake.
但最棒的是那个带吊扇、正对湖面的巨大带顶露台。

299
00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:18.370
Oh, and there's a mama cat and two little kittens living under the house next door to us.
哦，我们隔壁房子下面住着一只母猫和两只小猫。

300
00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.870
It is very hard not to rescue these kittens.
要忍住不去救助这些小猫真的太难了。

301
00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:27.810
They seem to be around the same age we usually get them to foster, right on the brink of being able to still be domesticated.
它们看起来和我们平时寄养的年纪差不多，正处于还能被驯化的边缘。

302
00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.350
The mom is young.
猫妈妈很年轻。

303
00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:33.690
I think the best we can do is put out some wet food while we're here to help her produce milk.
我觉得我们能做的最好的事，就是在我们在这儿的时候放一些湿粮，帮她分泌乳汁。

304
00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:34.450
Aw.
噢。

305
00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:35.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

306
00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:36.330
All right.
好啦。

307
00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.330
Are you ready for morning two?
准备好迎接第二天了吗？

308
00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:38.830
Yeah.
嗯。

309
00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:39.450
Yeah.
嗯。

310
00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.190
Well, yesterday was your quintessential lake day.
昨天可以说是极其典型的一天湖畔度假。

311
00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:46.830
Swimming, boat ride, trip to the grocery store for some item we forgot to bring with us.
游泳、坐船、为了买漏带的东西去了一趟杂货铺。

312
00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:47.490
More swimming.
继续游泳。

313
00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:48.650
My dad's barbecue.
我爸的烧烤。

314
00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:49.610
Family game.
家庭游戏。

315
00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:50.150
World Cup.
世界杯。

316
00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.070
We played the game Celebrity.
我们玩了“名人生死斗”这个游戏。

317
00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:55.970
There were nine of us playing, and it was pretty cool to play with three generations.
我们有九个人一起玩，三代人一块儿玩感觉挺酷的。

318
00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.790
We had names like Richard Chamberlain.
我们抽到了理查德·张伯伦这样的名字。

319
00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:00.590
Mm, that stumped the kids.
嗯，这把孩子们难住了。

320
00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:01.930
Which the kids did not know.
孩子们根本不认识。

321
00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.490
To Millie Bobby Brown, who my parents did not know.
还有米莉·波比·布朗，我爸妈则不认识她。

322
00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:10.430
But what I found really interesting are the celebrities that ended up in the bowl multiple times.
但我发现真正有趣的是，有些名人最后在签筒里出现了好几次。

323
00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:15.690
I'm not sure what it says about their fame, but Will Ferrell was in the bowl four times.
我不太确定这说明了他们有多出名，但威尔·法瑞尔在签筒里出现了四次。

324
00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:16.090
Oh.
哦。

325
00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:19.590
Madonna and Sabrina Carpenter were both in there three times.
麦当娜和萨布丽娜·卡彭特都在里面出现了三次。

326
00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:23.390
There were also two Michael Jacksons and two Barack Obamas.
还有两个迈克尔·杰克逊和两个贝拉克·奥巴马。

327
00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.930
We divided up girls against the boys, and the girls won.
我们按女生对男生分组对抗，最后女生赢了。

328
00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.010
Handily.
赢得轻轻松松。

329
00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:28.850
Oh.
哦。

330
00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:29.870
Handily.
轻轻松松。

331
00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.130
This morning, we all slept into 10 a.m.
今天早上，我们一直睡到上午10点。

332
00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:34.990
Glorious.
太美妙了。

333
00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.430
To our body clocks, that is 8 a.m.
按我们的生理钟算，那是早上8点。

334
00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:38.710
LA time, but still.
洛杉矶时间，但不管怎样。

335
00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:42.010
Have I said the bed in my Airbnb is super comfy?
我说过我短租房里的床超级舒服吗？

336
00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:47.410
With a ceiling fan, which is kind of the best thing ever if you have hot flashes.
还带有吊扇，如果你有潮热的毛病，这简直是世界上最棒的东西了。

337
00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.090
It's making me want to put a ceiling fan in at home.
这让我很想在家也装个吊扇。

338
00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:56.390
I woke up to a text from my sister that she and my mom were going to go to the local thrift store called Hope House.
我醒来时看到我姐发来的一条短信，说她和妈妈打算去当地一家叫“希望之家”的旧货店。

339
00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:00.410
My mom had some donations to drop off, and she also just loves looking around.
我妈有些捐赠物要送过去，而且她也很喜欢到处逛逛。

340
00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:04.630
My sister said my dad was going to Walmart to grab something, not sure what.
我姐说我爸要去沃尔玛买点东西，具体买什么不清楚。

341
00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:10.650
And yet, as of noon, my sister and my mom have still not gone to Hope House, which is pretty typical.
然而，直到中午，我姐和我妈还是没去“希望之家”，这也挺符合她们的一贯作风。

342
00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:15.650
First of all, they realized that the donations they wanted to drop off were in my dad's car,
首先，她们发现想捐的东西在我爸的车里，

343
00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.230
so they had to wait for him to get back from Walmart.
所以她们得等他从沃尔玛回来。

344
00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.530
However, there's a little bit of shade.
不过，这其中带有一点阴阳怪气。

345
00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:24.110
It's just a scooch of shade.
就那么一点点阴阳怪气。

346
00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.690
Every tenth word is a dagger.
每十个字里就有一把暗箭。

347
00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:26.230
Which is typical.
这也是家常便饭了。

348
00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:27.130
Yeah.
是啊。

349
00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:28.630
I mean, it is, though.
我的意思是，确实如此。

350
00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:36.890
I guess I'm super, like, braggy and shady in my journal with my family.
我猜我在日记里写到家人时，表现得超级自大又阴阳怪气。

351
00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:38.310
You know what?
你知道吗？

352
00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:45.230
The boys were all, like, thinking they were going to crush us in Celebrity, and they did not win, and they very much did not win.
那些男生之前一个个都觉得他们能在“名人猜猜看”游戏里把我们秒杀，结果他们没赢，而且是输得彻彻底底。

353
00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.310
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

354
00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.190
And now, did your mom and sister ever make it to the grocery store?
话说回来，你妈和你姐去成超市了吗？

355
00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:50.390
I'll let you know.
我一会儿告诉你。

356
00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.710
I will let you know.
我会告诉你的。

357
00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.070
You have to wait for it.
你得等等看。

358
00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.310
But this is the thing.
但关键是这样的。

359
00:16:54.470 --> 00:17:00.510
Like, they'll tell us, oh, the plan for the day is we're going to Hope House at 10 a.m., and then at noon, no one has left.
比如说，他们会告诉我们，哦，今天的计划是上午10点去希望之家，然后到了中午，根本没人出门。

360
00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:02.870
This is, like, very typical of my family.
这简直太符合我们家的一贯风格了。

361
00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:03.630
All right.
好吧。

362
00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.670
So, anyway, the problem was the stuff was in my dad's car.
所以呢，问题在于东西在我爸的车里。

363
00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.370
They had to wait for him to get back from Walmart.
他们得等他从沃尔玛回来。

364
00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:14.270
They dropped the kids at our place at 12.15, so the cousins are reunited and watching the World Cup.
他们12点15分把孩子送到了我们这儿，所以表兄弟们团聚了，正在看世界杯。

365
00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:18.170
And just now, my sister texted me that they made it to Hope House.
就在刚才，我姐发短信告诉我他们到希望之家了。

366
00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.190
It's 1 p.m.
现在下午1点。

367
00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:20.290
It's close.
这很接近了。

368
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.960
They're coming back home.
他们正在回家路上。

369
00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:30.140
My sister said, Mom, the sign clearly says they are open Monday, Wednesday, and Friday.
我姐说，妈，牌子上明明写着他们周一、周三和周五开门。

370
00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:31.380
This was a Tuesday.
可那天是周二。

371
00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:36.740
But my mom's response was, yeah, that's what the sign says, but sometimes they're open on Tuesdays.
但我妈的反应是，对啊，牌子上是这么写的，但他们有时周二也开门。

372
00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:37.820
They drove all the way there.
他们大老远开车去了那里。

373
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:41.900
I spent the morning reading a play by Gina Gianfrido.
我一上午都在读吉娜·吉安弗里多的剧本。

374
00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:43.980
I hope I'm saying her name right.
希望我没念错她的名字。

375
00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:49.640
When we were in New York, we saw the revival of her play Becky Shaw, which I absolutely loved.
我们在纽约时，看她的复排剧《贝基·肖》，我超级喜欢。

376
00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:53.320
So, now I'm reading her other plays because I love living in her dialogue.
所以，我现在在读她的其他剧本，因为我太喜欢沉浸在她的对白里了。

377
00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:59.860
Oh, I just finished the book Yesteryear, which was a trip and a great summer page turner.
哦，我刚读完《昔日》那本书，真是一段奇妙的旅程，也是一本适合夏日一口气读完的好书。

378
00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:01.640
It's kind of the book of the moment.
这算是当下最火的书了。

379
00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:07.900
It's about a trad wife influencer who suddenly wakes up living an actual pioneer life like in the 1800s.
讲的是一个传统娇妻网红突然醒来，过上了19世纪那种真正的拓荒生活。

380
00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.340
I read All Fours by Miranda July earlier this year,
我今年早些时候读了米兰达·朱莱的《全四方》，

381
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.780
and I feel like reading them both in the same year was very interesting.
我觉得同年读这两本书非常有意思。

382
00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.920
In both instances, the protagonists are women who feel suffocated by what they perceive to be
在这两部作品中，女主角都感到被她们所认为的

383
00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:22.500
the confines of living a married life with children.
为人妻母的婚姻生活束缚得喘不过气来。

384
00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.060
Very, very different protagonists, but similar theme.
两位主角非常非常不同，但主题相似。

385
00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.400
They would make an interesting addition to a women's studies course.
把它们加入妇女研究课程会是个有趣的补充。

386
00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:32.460
Jenna, again, I'm on the same book train as you.
珍娜，又来了，我和你看的是同一本书。

387
00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:33.340
You are?
是吗？

388
00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:38.020
Yeah, you and I are three for three on Marriage at Sea, Strangers, and Yesteryear.
对啊，你和我对《海上婚姻》、《陌生人》和《昔日》这三本的看法完全一致。

389
00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.540
Matt, what did you think of Yesteryear?
马特，你觉得《昔日》怎么样？

390
00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.020
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

391
00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.640
I thought it was so interesting and funny.
我觉得它非常有意思又好笑。

392
00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.420
And I don't know, just kind of right on,
而且怎么说呢，就觉得很贴切，

393
00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.600
kind of a different perspective than I would normally have.
带有一种我平时不会有的独特视角。

394
00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:50.580
I agree.
我同意。

395
00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.200
I really, really liked it.
我是真的真的很喜欢。

396
00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.180
It was quite a page turner.
它确实是一本让人手不释卷的书。

397
00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:55.120
I think I tore through that in about four days.
我想我大概四天就把它读完了。

398
00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:56.440
Yeah, totally.
对，完全同意。

399
00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:57.400
Let's discuss.
我们来讨论一下吧。

400
00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:58.620
We can discuss more.
我们可以深入讨论一下。

401
00:18:59.080 --> 00:18:59.720
All right.
好的。

402
00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.040
I go on to say,
接着我要说的是，

403
00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:05.880
but the book I finished recently that has become perhaps my all-time favorite book ever
但我最近读完的那本书，或许已经成为了我历年来最喜欢的书

404
00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.020
is Station Eleven.
那就是《站前十一》。y

405
00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:11.580
In the same way that Demon Copperhead created a fundamental shift in my awareness,
就像《恶魔科普海德》彻底改变了我的认知一样，

406
00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:15.040
Station Eleven has too, but on an even deeper level.
《站前十一》也是如此，但在更深层次上。

407
00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.340
It is a story of a flu that wipes out 99% of humanity.
这是一个关于一场流感消灭了百分之九十九人类的故事。

408
00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:23.240
With only 1% of people left, all industry has stopped.
只剩下百分之一的人，所有工业都停摆了。

409
00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:26.040
All electricity, food production, transportation.
所有的电力、食品生产、交通都停了。

410
00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:31.240
The story centers around a few characters and their experiences in these new times.
故事围绕几个角色以及他们在这些新时代的经历展开。

411
00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:35.520
One of the main characters is a member of a troupe of musicians and actors
其中一个主要角色是一个音乐家和演员剧团的成员，

412
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:39.500
who go from settlement to settlement performing Shakespeare and playing music.
他们挨个定居点巡回演出莎士比亚戏剧和音乐。

413
00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:44.720
Their commitment to creating art in a world of survival is intensely beautiful.
他们在生存世界中对创造艺术的执着美得令人窒息。

414
00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:48.020
They quote a line from Star Trek as their motto,
他们引用《星际迷航》里的一句台词作为座右铭，

415
00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:48.640
quote,
引号，

416
00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.900
because survival is insufficient,
因为单单生存是不够的，

417
00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.780
which is now maybe my favorite quote ever.
这现在可能成了我最喜欢的名言。

418
00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:56.700
It was a spiritual experience for me.
对我来说这是一次精神洗礼。

419
00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:59.620
It had me pondering what it means to be human,
它让我思考作为人类意味着什么，

420
00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:04.140
the ways in which we are all interconnected during our passage of time on Earth.
我们在地球上度过时光时彼此相连的方式。

421
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:09.740
There is one paragraph about a snow globe that is now my favorite piece of writing.
有一段关于雪球的段落现在成了我最喜欢的文字。

422
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.500
I will never forget it.
我永远不会忘记它。

423
00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.800
I've gone back to it a few times since finishing the book.
自从读完这本书后，我又回去读了好几次。

424
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:18.440
When I read it over again, I feel a deep ache in my stomach
当我再次阅读时，我的胃部会隐隐作痛，

425
00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:22.260
because what it evokes is so beautiful, it's hard to hold in my body.
因为那种唤起的情感太美了，几乎无法承受。

426
00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:25.800
I will never see a snow globe the same way again.
我再也不会用以前的眼光看待雪球了。

427
00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:28.380
My goodness, I need to read that.
天哪，我得去读读那本书。

428
00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:32.400
It's absolutely wonderful.
这绝对太棒了。

429
00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:35.720
All right, moving on.
好了，继续。

430
00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.060
I wrote moving on.
我写了继续。

431
00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:39.000
Moving on, I have a cat update.
接下来，我有个猫咪近况更新。

432
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:44.600
We fed the mama three meals of wet food yesterday and also left out dry food overnight.
我们昨天给猫妈妈喂了三顿湿粮，晚上还留了干粮。

433
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.360
It was all gone in the morning.
早上全都吃光了。

434
00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.640
She ate well yesterday, but no sign of her babies.
她昨天吃得很好，但没看到她的小猫。

435
00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:55.180
Yesterday afternoon, I saw two lake otters also living under the house next door.
昨天下午，我看到两只水獭也住在隔壁房子下面。

436
00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.000
These people have a small petting zoo living under their deck.
这些人家的露台底下居然住着一个小型的抚摸动物园。

437
00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:01.320
I also saw a bunch of geese down by their dock this morning.
今天早上我还看到他们码头边有一群大雁。

438
00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:06.420
Oh, and my folks have a pair of ducks that swim with us and we can feed them out of our hands.
哦，我爸妈有一对鸭子会和我们一起游泳，我们还能用手喂它们。

439
00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.500
We are also seeing a ton of deer.
我们还看到了大量的鹿。

440
00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:10.380
Lots of animals at the lake.
湖边有好多动物。

441
00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:11.200
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

442
00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.040
All right.
好的。

443
00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:15.020
Next day.
第二天。

444
00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:16.680
Lake day three.
湖畔第三天。

445
00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:18.420
Good morning!
大家早上好！

446
00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:22.020
Somebody slept well.
有人睡得真香。

447
00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:24.960
Have I mentioned how much I liked this?
我提过我有多喜欢这个吗？

448
00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:25.400
Exactly.
没错。

449
00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:30.920
When we got back to the house last night, the mama cat ran over to the edge of our porch expectantly.
昨晚我们回到屋里时，猫妈妈满怀期待地跑到了我们门廊边缘。

450
00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.720
We put out some wet food and her two kittens also came up to eat.
我们放了一些湿粮，她的两只小猫也上来吃了。

451
00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:37.580
This is when we got our first really good look at them.
这就是我们真正看清它们长相的时候。

452
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.480
The mama is a gray tabby.
猫妈妈是一只灰色虎斑猫。

453
00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:43.480
She has a gray tabby lookalike kitten, except that her baby has white paws.
它有一只长相酷似它的灰色虎斑小猫，只不过小猫长着白色的爪子。

454
00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:46.460
And then there is a super shy, smaller, all black kitten.
然后还有一只超级害羞、个头更小、全身漆黑的小猫。

455
00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:49.480
I fed them three plates of wet food.
我给它们喂了三盘湿粮。

456
00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:50.880
They could not get enough.
它们怎么也吃不够。

457
00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.780
My daughter is angling for us to take them back to St. Louis.
我女儿正变着法儿想让我们把它们带回圣路易斯。

458
00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.240
She looked up the rules for flying them home.
她查阅了把它们带上飞机的规定。

459
00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.180
I told her that pets must be up to date for their shots in order to fly,
我告诉她，宠物必须打完最新的疫苗才能坐飞机，

460
00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:02.340
but she said she read online that, quote,
但她说她在网上看到，原话是，

461
00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:04.640
a lot of times Southwest doesn't even check.
很多时候西南航空甚至都不会检查。

462
00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:05.440
Oh, no.
哦，不。

463
00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:06.840
I said, quote,
我说，原话是，

464
00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:10.040
I'm not going to try and take three feral cats on an airplane,
我是绝不会尝试带三只野猫坐飞机的，

465
00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:13.740
but I'm feeling the same urge to rescue them as she is.
但我跟她一样，也有一种想要救助它们的冲动。

466
00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:16.640
When you have a skill, which for us is cat rescue,
当你具备某种技能时，对我们来说就是救助猫咪，

467
00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:18.980
it's hard not to put that skill into action.
你很难不去付诸行动。

468
00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:23.340
I also woke up realizing that this is our last full day here,
我醒来时还意识到，这是我们在这里的最后一个完整的一天，

469
00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:25.780
which means my last full day with my folks.
这也意味着我跟父母在一起的最后一个完整的一天。

470
00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:27.720
My dad is getting older.
我爸爸年纪越来越大了。

471
00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:32.740
He turns 80 this year, and I'm always acutely aware that I'm on borrowed time with them.
他今年就满80岁了，我总是深深地意识到我和他们在一起的日子是在偷来的时光。

472
00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:37.440
I want to ask them more questions, but I'm not sure what those questions are.
我想问他们更多问题，但我不知道该问些什么。

473
00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:42.860
Mostly, I just want to drink them in, particularly my dad here at the lake.
总的来说，我只想好好端详他们，尤其是这里湖边的爸爸。

474
00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:47.400
He's always puttering around, doing little chores, even at his age.
他总是东忙西忙，做些零碎的杂务，尽管他已经这把年纪了。

475
00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:51.280
Making barbecue ribs for dinner last night was a whole day affair.
昨天花了一整天的时间来做晚饭吃的烤排骨。

476
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.980
It's multiple steps.
步骤很多。

477
00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:55.960
I'm noticing him in every detail here,
我注意到他这里的每一个细节，

478
00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:59.120
like all the do-it-yourself fixes to little problems,
比如对各种小问题的DIY修复，

479
00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:03.120
like how he has a special spot to tie up the swim noodles on the dock,
比如他在码头上怎么弄了个专用地方来绑游泳面条，

480
00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:07.620
or the sunshade he puts on hooks outside their bedroom window for when the sun is setting.
或者太阳落山时，他挂在卧室窗户外面的遮阳篷。

481
00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:10.040
I'm trying to drink it all in.
我正努力把这一切都印在脑海里。

482
00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:12.580
Yesterday was another typical lake day.
昨天是又一个典型的湖畔日。

483
00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.660
Tubing, boat rides, swimming, my dad's delicious barbecue ribs for dinner,
玩滑水圈、坐船兜风、游泳、晚餐有爸爸做的美味烤排骨，

484
00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:20.140
my mom's homemade coleslaw, or as she says, cold slaw.
妈妈做的自制凉拌卷心菜，或者按她的话说是冷卷心菜。

485
00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:22.520
Another game of celebrity.
又玩了一局名人猜猜看。

486
00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:24.220
This time, the boys won.
这一次，男孩们赢了。

487
00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:26.540
We said we need to do a tiebreaker tonight.
我们说今晚得来场决胜局。

488
00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:30.780
By the way, I'm sorry to George Clooney, but none of the kids knew who he was.
顺便说一句，我对乔治·克鲁尼感到抱歉，但孩子们中没有一个知道他是谁。

489
00:23:32.420 --> 00:23:34.480
Last night, we also did fireworks.
昨晚，我们还放了烟花。

490
00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:38.960
They are illegal in Los Angeles, and it's super fun for the kids to do them each year
它们在洛杉矶是非法的，孩子们每年在湖边和表兄弟姐妹们一起放烟花，

491
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:40.160
with their cousins at the lake.
觉得超级好玩。

492
00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:44.260
On our drive down, we passed by so many firework stands on the side of the road.
在我们开车南下的路上，我们路过了路边的好多烟花摊。

493
00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:47.180
It's such a core memory of my childhood around the 4th of July,
路边烟花摊是我对7月4日国庆日童年记忆的核心部分。

494
00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:49.260
the roadside firework stand.
路边烟花摊。

495
00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:53.940
We got ours from a little place in front of a gas station near my folks' lake house.
我们的烟花是从我父母湖边住宅附近加油站前面的一家小店买的。

496
00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:57.000
We got the usual, chicken, tank, fountains.
我们买了常规的，小鸡、坦克、喷泉烟花。

497
00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:00.360
Then we went outside the box and got something called big blue balls,
然后我们不走寻常路，买了一种叫大蓝球的东西，

498
00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:02.560
and one that was shaped like a Slurpee.
还有一个形状像思乐冰的烟花。

499
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:06.580
And then we asked the guy at the stand what would make a good finale,
接着我们问摊位老板什么东西适合做压轴，

500
00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:10.260
and he pointed us to this giant pack of rockets for like $200.
他给我们推荐了一大包价值200美元左右的火箭弹。

501
00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:12.360
Did you get them?
你买到了吗？

502
00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:13.080
No.
没有。

503
00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:15.340
We said, quote, a smaller finale.
我们当时说的是，引用原话，一个更小的压轴节目。

504
00:24:16.520 --> 00:24:19.600
We settled on this cube with a dinosaur on it.
我们最后选了这个印有恐龙图案的方盒。

505
00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:22.100
It was supposed to have 10 shots inside.
它里面本来应该有10发。

506
00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:23.280
He said it would be good.
他说这个会很不错。

507
00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:26.080
We had the kids arrange everything in an order.
我们让孩子们按顺序把所有东西排好。

508
00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:27.420
We started with the chicken.
我们从“小鸡”开始。

509
00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:28.900
It was lame, as expected.
不出所料，挺没劲的。

510
00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:30.640
Small tank was lame.
小号水雷很无聊。

511
00:24:30.880 --> 00:24:31.900
Medium tank was cool.
中号水雷挺酷的。

512
00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:34.940
The exploding blue balls was a fun surprise.
爆炸的蓝色气球是个有趣的惊喜。

513
00:24:35.400 --> 00:24:36.320
Slurpee was awesome.
“思乐冰”太棒了。

514
00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:36.980
That's what she said.
她刚才就是这么说的。

515
00:24:40.740 --> 00:24:41.900
It's very funny.
这非常搞笑。

516
00:24:42.620 --> 00:24:43.740
Slurpee was awesome.
“思乐冰”太棒了。

517
00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:44.960
The fountains were fountains.
喷泉也就是那么回事。

518
00:24:45.560 --> 00:24:47.260
Then we set up dino box.
然后我们布置了恐龙盒。

519
00:24:47.480 --> 00:24:50.240
I would like to repeat that this box was small.
我想再次强调，这个盒子很小。

520
00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:53.200
Like, imagine if a softball was a cube.
就想象一下，如果一个垒球是个正方体。

521
00:24:53.380 --> 00:24:55.060
You could hold it in one hand for sure.
你绝对可以单手把它拿住。

522
00:24:55.060 --> 00:25:01.340
I think we were expecting like 10 smallish fireworks to fly up one by one overhead and explode, kind
我想我们当时期待的是，大概10个不太大的烟花依次飞上头顶爆炸，有点

523
00:25:01.340 --> 00:25:03.300
of like bottle rockets, but a little better.
像窜天猴，但要更好一点。

524
00:25:03.860 --> 00:25:08.600
Dear Lord, this thing was like a tiny professional fireworks show in a cube.
我的天哪，这东西简直就像是一个装在方盒里的微型专业烟花秀。

525
00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:11.180
And it wasn't 10 of the same thing either.
而且它也不是10个完全相同的烟花。

526
00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:17.620
It was this intense variety of different giant fireworks shooting into the air literally right
里面是各种各样极其丰富的巨大烟花，铺天盖地地射向空中，

527
00:25:17.620 --> 00:25:18.260
above us.
就在我们头顶上方。

528
00:25:18.440 --> 00:25:20.820
It was completely unexpected and a great finale.
这完全出乎意料，而且是个相当棒的压轴。

529
00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:21.860
Oh, awesome.
哦，太棒了。

530
00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:22.560
That's great.
那太好了。

531
00:25:23.060 --> 00:25:23.440
All right.
好吧。

532
00:25:23.780 --> 00:25:25.200
Final Lake Day, everybody.
各位，这是在湖畔的最后一天。

533
00:25:25.200 --> 00:25:28.100
Our final full day at the lake was a big success.
我们在湖边的最后一个完整的一天非常成功。

534
00:25:28.480 --> 00:25:31.340
My mom and sister made it back to Hope House in the morning.
我妈和我姐早上赶回了希望之家。

535
00:25:31.900 --> 00:25:36.600
It was a Wednesday and they were in fact open, as the sign suggested.
那天是周三，正如招牌上所说，他们确实开门营业了。

536
00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:40.740
My mom dropped off her donations and got my dad a nice summer shirt.
我妈放下捐赠物，给我爸买了一件漂亮的夏日衬衫。

537
00:25:40.740 --> 00:25:42.060
She loves a good find.
她就喜欢淘到好东西。

538
00:25:42.460 --> 00:25:45.880
We rented a wave runner and hosted everyone at our place.
我们租了一艘水上摩托艇，并在我们的住处招待了所有人。

539
00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:50.940
My folks brought over a bunch of lunch stuff and a cooler and drinks and we basically camped
我父母带了许多午餐用品、一个冷藏箱还有饮料，我们基本上整天

540
00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:52.080
out on our dock all day.
都扎营在我们的码头上了。

541
00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:56.660
I should mention that the one drawback to our rental is that the house is up high on
我得提一下，我们租的房子唯一的缺点是建在

542
00:25:56.660 --> 00:25:57.020
a hill.
小山的高处。

543
00:25:57.200 --> 00:26:02.200
There are multiple levels of decks leading down to the water and lots and lots and lots
有多层露台通往水边，还有数不清、数不清、数不清

544
00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:02.760
of stairs.
的台阶。

545
00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:08.100
Once you get down there, you only want to go back to the house if you absolutely need something.
一旦你下去了，除非万不得已，否则你根本不想回屋里去。

546
00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:12.260
There are so many stairs you might consider pooping in the lake.
台阶多到你甚至会考虑在湖里拉屎。

547
00:26:13.460 --> 00:26:16.780
Thankfully, it never came to that, but I'm just saying it was a climb.
好在还没到那一步，但我只是说，爬上去可真够呛。

548
00:26:16.960 --> 00:26:19.800
We tried hard to have everything we needed down on the dock.
我们尽最大努力把需要的东西都备在码头上。

549
00:26:20.300 --> 00:26:24.500
When we did need something from the house, I'd volunteer to go and get it as I decided
当我们确实需要从屋里拿什么东西时，我会主动申请去拿，因为我决定

550
00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:28.600
that the stairs and treading water were my two chances at exercise during this trip.
爬楼梯和在水中踩水是我这次旅行中仅有的两次锻炼机会。

551
00:26:28.960 --> 00:26:32.720
All day long, we basically took turns riding the wave runner and swimming.
一整天里，我们基本上轮流玩水上摩托艇和游泳。

552
00:26:33.220 --> 00:26:36.080
Our dock also had a diving platform that the kids loved.
我们的码头还有一个跳水平台，孩子们特别喜欢。

553
00:26:36.420 --> 00:26:39.720
Lots of near heart attacks for me watching them flip and dive off that thing.
看着他们从那上面翻腾跳水，我差点心脏病发好几次。

554
00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:43.920
In the evening, we ordered takeout and watched the USA World Cup game together.
傍晚时分，我们叫了外卖，一起观看美国队的世界杯比赛。

555
00:26:44.260 --> 00:26:48.120
Me and my folks sat outside on the covered patio and watched the outside TV.
我和我爸妈坐在带顶棚的露台外面，看着室外的电视。

556
00:26:48.120 --> 00:26:52.400
They weren't super interested in the game, so it gave me a good chance to ask some questions
他们对比赛不是特别感兴趣，这正好给了我一个好机会问几个问题，

557
00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:54.880
and get the scoop on the lake house and how it came about.
顺便打听一下这座湖畔别墅的来历和建造过程。

558
00:26:55.280 --> 00:26:57.540
I found out my memory was mostly correct.
我发现我的记忆大体上是准确的。

559
00:26:57.840 --> 00:27:00.920
They bought the land when I was eight years old and it took a year to build.
他们在我八岁那年买下了这块地，花了一年时间才建好。

560
00:27:01.380 --> 00:27:04.920
My dad told me he especially liked that the house faced weSt.
我爸告诉我，他特别喜欢这座房子朝西的朝向。

561
00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:09.420
He wanted to sit on the deck in the mornings and have coffee without the sun in his eyes.
他想在早晨坐在露台上喝咖啡，免得阳光晃眼。

562
00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:14.220
Since this is literally one of my favorite things to do at the lake, I love knowing that detail.
既然这简直是我在湖边最喜欢做的事情之一，听到这个细节我真的很开心。

563
00:27:14.720 --> 00:27:19.100
He also told me the man they hired to build the house was a drunk and they got into a ton
他还告诉我，他们雇来建房子的那个男人是个酒鬼，他们为此吵了无数次

564
00:27:19.100 --> 00:27:19.600
of fights.
架。

565
00:27:20.300 --> 00:27:22.100
He would set a meeting with my dad.
他会约我爸见面。

566
00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:26.120
My dad would drive three hours from St. Louis and then the guy would be late and reek of
我爸从圣路易斯开车开三个小时过来，结果那家伙迟到而且满身

567
00:27:26.120 --> 00:27:26.600
booze.
酒气。

568
00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:28.160
It caused a lot of probleMs.
这引发了很多问题。

569
00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:32.760
At one point, they got into such a huge argument, the man threatened to burn the house down.
有一次，他们吵得那么厉害，那家伙甚至威胁要把房子烧了。

570
00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:33.680
Oh my goodness.
我的天呐。

571
00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:34.200
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

572
00:27:35.340 --> 00:27:38.060
In other news, we met the neighbor next door to our rental.
说点别的，我们遇到了出租屋隔壁的邻居。

573
00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:42.020
I mentioned that he had some stray cats living under his porch and that we'd been feeding
我提到他门廊底下住着几只流浪猫，我们一直在喂

574
00:27:42.020 --> 00:27:42.280
them.
它们。

575
00:27:42.520 --> 00:27:45.600
I offered to give him our leftover food if he'd like to keep feeding them.
我提出如果他想继续喂它们，可以把我们吃剩的食物给他。

576
00:27:45.680 --> 00:27:47.320
And he said his wife already feeds them.
结果他说他妻子已经在喂了。

577
00:27:47.440 --> 00:27:48.900
We were so excited to hear this.
听到这个消息我们太兴奋了。

578
00:27:49.200 --> 00:27:53.060
