00:34:29.720 --> 00:34:30.500
What a trip.
真是了不起的旅程。

719
00:34:30.920 --> 00:34:31.880
That's amazing.
太神奇了。

720
00:34:32.260 --> 00:34:33.180
I love it.
我喜欢。

721
00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:33.640
Yeah.
对。

722
00:34:34.340 --> 00:34:34.740
All right.
好啦。

723
00:34:34.820 --> 00:34:35.740
Well, should we take a break?
那我们是不是该休息一下？

724
00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:38.820
And then we'll be back, Angela, with your Wimbledon share.
等会儿我们回来，安吉拉，你会分享温网的经历。

725
00:34:39.060 --> 00:34:41.020
And Sam is going to share about Germany.
然后萨姆要分享关于德国的事情。

726
00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:41.460
Yeah.
对。

727
00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:43.220
We both went abroad.
我们两个都出国了。

728
00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:43.680
Yeah.
对。

729
00:34:43.880 --> 00:34:44.020
Yeah.
对。

730
00:34:44.500 --> 00:34:44.980
Right.
没错。

731
00:34:54.510 --> 00:34:55.370
We are back.
我们回来了。

732
00:34:55.370 --> 00:34:58.690
And I have been waiting a few weeks to hear about your trip to Wimbledon.
我等你的温网之旅已经等了好几个星期了。

733
00:34:58.830 --> 00:34:59.970
I can wait no longer.
我再也等不下去了。

734
00:35:00.210 --> 00:35:00.750
I'm on the edge of my seat.
我都急不可耐了。

735
00:35:00.750 --> 00:35:04.670
You guys, I made her go second because I knew this was the journal.
伙计们，我让她第二个讲，因为我知道这就是那本日志。

736
00:35:04.990 --> 00:35:05.110
Yeah.
对。

737
00:35:05.110 --> 00:35:05.350
Yeah.
对。

738
00:35:05.390 --> 00:35:06.250
You can't follow this.
你根本没法接着这个讲。

739
00:35:06.590 --> 00:35:07.070
I don't think so.
我觉得也是。

740
00:35:07.470 --> 00:35:09.210
Jenna's and Matt's were both wonderful.
珍娜和马特的都很精彩。

741
00:35:09.390 --> 00:35:12.750
Mine, I don't think it's that interesting, but I'm going to read it.
我的嘛，我觉得没那么有趣，不过我还是会读给大家听。

742
00:35:13.010 --> 00:35:17.110
First of all, I want you guys to know I've been to London many times and I did a semester
首先，我想让大家知道，我去过伦敦很多次，大学时还在伦敦当过一学期

743
00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:19.270
abroad in college in London.
交换生。

744
00:35:19.270 --> 00:35:22.350
So I didn't need to do a ton of tourist stuff.
所以我不怎么需要去搞什么观光旅游。

745
00:35:22.570 --> 00:35:26.370
This was really about seeing my friends, hanging out with my friends that live there, and then
这次主要是为了见朋友，和住在那里的朋友们一起玩，然后

746
00:35:26.370 --> 00:35:28.750
ending the trip with us all going to Wimbledon.
以我们大家一起去温网作为旅程的收尾。

747
00:35:28.750 --> 00:35:31.150
So anyway, just thought I would preface that.
总之，我就是先做个铺垫。

748
00:35:31.330 --> 00:35:31.430
Okay.
好吧。

749
00:35:31.730 --> 00:35:32.210
All right.
行吧。

750
00:35:32.370 --> 00:35:34.450
This is titled AK Travel Journal.
这篇的标题是《AK旅游日志》。

751
00:35:34.670 --> 00:35:35.010
Okay.
好吧。

752
00:35:35.170 --> 00:35:36.870
I don't know why I felt the need to title it.
我不知道为什么觉得非得给它起个标题不可。

753
00:35:37.290 --> 00:35:38.350
And here it goes.
要开始了。

754
00:35:38.550 --> 00:35:40.950
Tuesday, June 30th, 1130 a.m.
6月30日星期二，上午11点30分。

755
00:35:41.070 --> 00:35:42.330
On the way to the airport.
在去机场的路上。

756
00:35:42.570 --> 00:35:43.730
So excited.
太激动了。

757
00:35:44.130 --> 00:35:44.610
Woohoo!
呜呼！

758
00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:52.710
We are behind a 1990 silver Toyota Corolla that has pinstriping that says Gnocchi Mobile.
我们前面有一辆1990年的银色丰田花冠，车身侧面有写着“玉棋号”的细条纹装饰。

759
00:35:53.750 --> 00:35:57.390
How much do you have to love Gnocchi to pinstripe it on your car?
得有多爱玉棋，才会把它画在车身上啊？

760
00:35:58.470 --> 00:36:00.250
Hi from the TSA line.
来自机场安检排队处的问候。

761
00:36:00.430 --> 00:36:04.690
So we play this game with our kids when we travel, where we share things you overhear
所以我们旅行时跟孩子们玩过这样一个游戏，就是分享你走路时无意中听到的话

762
00:36:04.690 --> 00:36:05.790
as you walk past someone.
从某人身边走过时听到的。

763
00:36:06.050 --> 00:36:08.750
This started a few years back on a trip to New York City.
这始于几年前去纽约市的一次旅行。

764
00:36:08.950 --> 00:36:13.910
A big city is great for this game because you hear crazy snippets of people's conversations
大城市非常适合玩这个游戏，因为你能听到别人谈话的疯狂片段

765
00:36:13.910 --> 00:36:15.610
as you walk past them on the street.
当你在街上从他们身边走过时。

766
00:36:16.090 --> 00:36:18.130
But it is also fun at airports.
但在机场玩也很有趣。

767
00:36:18.590 --> 00:36:21.390
Here's one of those moments from my walk through LAX.
这是我在洛杉矶国际机场走过时遇到的一个瞬间。

768
00:36:21.390 --> 00:36:26.570
This man had two suitcases and he was hauling ass to try to get to the front of the security
这个男人带着两个行李箱，他正全速赶路，试图在这一大群人到达之前冲到安检队伍的前面

769
00:36:26.570 --> 00:36:28.990
line before this big group got there.
队伍到了那里。

770
00:36:29.530 --> 00:36:32.310
Trailing behind him carrying a big bag was his wife.
跟在他后面提着一个大包的是他的妻子。

771
00:36:32.490 --> 00:36:36.230
She was clearly annoyed at his brisk pace and she said,
她对他的快节奏明显感到恼火，她说，

772
00:36:36.670 --> 00:36:38.930
Gary, can you slow your roll?
加里，你能放慢点节奏吗？

773
00:36:39.710 --> 00:36:41.290
That cracked me up.
这把我逗乐了。

774
00:36:42.570 --> 00:36:43.550
2 p.m.
下午2点。

775
00:36:43.710 --> 00:36:45.110
At the airport lounge, baby.
在机场贵宾室，宝贝。

776
00:36:46.750 --> 00:36:48.930
This is a bucket list trip for me.
对我和说这是一次列入人生愿望清单的旅行。

777
00:36:49.050 --> 00:36:50.850
So I went all out.
所以我全力以赴了。

778
00:36:51.070 --> 00:36:53.450
I used my miles and I'm flying business class.
我用了我的里程，坐的是商务舱。

779
00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:54.350
Ooh la la.
噢啦啦。

780
00:36:55.010 --> 00:36:57.710
I still can't believe I'm going to Wimbledon!
我还是不敢相信我要去温网了！

781
00:36:58.410 --> 00:36:59.610
Two exclamation points.
两个感叹号。

782
00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:03.530
I can't remember a summer where I didn't watch Wimbledon with my mom.
我不记得有哪个夏天我没有和妈妈一起看温网。

783
00:37:03.690 --> 00:37:05.210
It's her favorite tennis tournament.
这是她最喜欢的网球锦标赛。

784
00:37:05.430 --> 00:37:07.410
We have always dreamed of going together.
我们一直梦想着能一起去。

785
00:37:07.410 --> 00:37:11.650
We have spent countless hours in front of the TV watching all the matches.
我们花在电视机前看所有比赛的时间数不胜数。

786
00:37:11.830 --> 00:37:15.730
We would make ourselves cups of tea and eat strawberries and pretend we were there.
我们会给自己泡杯茶，吃着草莓，假装我们就身临其境。

787
00:37:15.930 --> 00:37:20.370
I have so many favorite moments like when Beyond Borg beat John McEnroe and he dropped
我有太多最喜欢的时刻，比如当比约恩·博格击败约翰·麦肯罗时，他双膝跪在草地上，或者塞雷纳·威廉姆斯多次获胜并用力挥舞拳头

788
00:37:20.370 --> 00:37:25.050
to his knees on the grass or the many times Serena Williams won and would pump her fists
就像太棒了那样。

789
00:37:25.050 --> 00:37:25.930
like hell yeah.
我妈妈最喜欢的球员之一是金·克里斯特尔斯。

790
00:37:26.330 --> 00:37:29.250
One of my mom's favorite players was Kim Clijsters.
我们很喜欢看她打球，这就是生活变得真正疯狂的地方。

791
00:37:29.570 --> 00:37:33.310
We loved watching her play and this is where life gets really crazy.
当我写下这些时，我仍然无法相信，但是

792
00:37:33.550 --> 00:37:36.570
And as I write this, I still can't believe it, but
我去年在国际网球名人堂遇到了金·克里斯特尔斯。

793
00:37:36.570 --> 00:37:40.550
I met Kim Clijsters last year at the International Tennis Hall of Fame.
她是最善良、最美好的人之一，更不用说网球史上的伟大人物之一了。

794
00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:46.090
She is one of the nicest, most wonderful people, not to mention one of the greats in tennis
在过去的一年里，我们一直保持着联系，并成为了朋友。

795
00:37:46.090 --> 00:37:46.450
history.
啊！

796
00:37:46.770 --> 00:37:49.950
We have stayed in touch over the past year and have become friends.
感叹号。

797
00:37:50.170 --> 00:37:50.530
Ah!
是不是很疯狂？

798
00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:52.810
Exclamation point.
我和妈妈至今都难以置信。

799
00:37:53.490 --> 00:37:55.090
Isn't that crazy?
是不是很疯狂？

800
00:37:55.510 --> 00:37:57.990
My mom and I both still can't believe it.
我和我妈现在都还不敢相信。

801
00:37:58.130 --> 00:38:02.310
I shared with Kim our love of Wimbledon and she offered to help me get tickets.
我跟金分享了我们对温网的热爱，她主动提出帮我搞到门票。

802
00:38:02.490 --> 00:38:04.030
I about fell on the floor.
我差点惊得摔倒在地上。

803
00:38:04.030 --> 00:38:06.950
Getting tickets to Wimbledon is really difficult.
买到温网的门票真的很难。

804
00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:08.390
I've never been able to.
我从来都没买到过。

805
00:38:08.670 --> 00:38:10.010
I called my mom immediately.
我立刻给我妈打了电话。

806
00:38:10.010 --> 00:38:13.310
She was so excited and I asked her to go with me.
她非常兴奋，我便邀请她跟我一起去。

807
00:38:14.050 --> 00:38:15.950
We had a really long conversation.
我们聊了很久很久。

808
00:38:16.450 --> 00:38:21.550
You know, my mom turned 88 this year and she shared with me that long travel days are just
你知道的，我妈今年88岁了，她跟我说长途奔波对她来说

809
00:38:21.550 --> 00:38:22.570
too much for her now.
现在实在是吃不消了。

810
00:38:23.250 --> 00:38:26.390
But she told me I absolutely had to go.
但她告诉我说我无论如何都得去。

811
00:38:26.570 --> 00:38:28.690
She said I had to go for the both of us.
她说我得代表我们俩去。

812
00:38:29.130 --> 00:38:33.350
And I had orders to take a ton of pictures and call her every day.
而且她下达了命令，让我拍大量的照片，并且每天都要给她打电话。

813
00:38:34.370 --> 00:38:36.090
So, this is going to make me cry.
所以，这快要把我弄哭了。

814
00:38:37.130 --> 00:38:42.790
Here I sit in the airport lounge texting my mom and wearing a necklace that my dad bought
此时我坐在机场休息室里，一边给妈妈发信息，一边戴着一条我爸爸在

815
00:38:42.790 --> 00:38:43.910
her in the 70s.
70年代买给她的项链。

816
00:38:44.010 --> 00:38:49.530
He knew her love of tennis and it's a string of tiny gold interlocking tennis rackets.
他知道她热爱网球，那是一串由微小黄金互扣而成的网球拍。

817
00:38:49.710 --> 00:38:55.230
My mom gave it to me after he passed away and I knew I had to wear it on this trip.
我爸爸去世后，我妈把它送给了我，我知道这次旅行我一定要戴着它。

818
00:38:55.650 --> 00:39:00.150
So, I'm going to hold her and my dad close to my heart as I go on this adventure.
所以，在我开启这段冒险时，我会把她和爸爸紧紧放在心底。

819
00:39:00.150 --> 00:39:09.010
We both were bumping up against our parents' age and limitations and our awareness of that
我们在旅行中都切实感受到了父母的年龄与局限，

820
00:39:09.010 --> 00:39:10.150
on our trips.
以及对这一点的清醒认识。

821
00:39:10.330 --> 00:39:10.690
Yes.
是的。

822
00:39:10.890 --> 00:39:11.150
Yeah.
对啊。

823
00:39:11.370 --> 00:39:17.370
It was so thrilling to get these tickets and also bittersweet that my mom wasn't with me,
能拿到这些门票让人无比激动，但同时又有点苦乐参半，因为我妈没能跟我一起来，

824
00:39:17.470 --> 00:39:18.210
but she was.
不过她其实也算陪着我。

825
00:39:18.590 --> 00:39:18.770
Yeah.
对。

826
00:39:18.990 --> 00:39:19.170
Okay.
好啦。

827
00:39:19.330 --> 00:39:19.730
Sorry.
不好意思。

828
00:39:19.910 --> 00:39:21.850
I needed to wipe the tears.
我得擦擦眼泪。

829
00:39:22.070 --> 00:39:24.530
And now, are you ready for a hard pivot?
那么现在，你们准备好迎接一个急转弯了吗？

830
00:39:24.770 --> 00:39:28.130
There had clearly been a passage in time because here's my next entry.
显然时间已经过去了一段，因为这是我的下一条记录。

831
00:39:28.330 --> 00:39:28.490
Ready?
准备好了吗？

832
00:39:28.670 --> 00:39:28.790
Okay.
好。

833
00:39:29.170 --> 00:39:29.990
Oh, Lord.
天呐。

834
00:39:30.150 --> 00:39:32.230
The man next to me took off his shoes.
我旁边的那位男士把鞋脱了。

835
00:39:33.730 --> 00:39:34.170
Why?
为什么？

836
00:39:35.190 --> 00:39:36.010
Oh, God.
哦，天哪。

837
00:39:36.190 --> 00:39:37.650
Now, he's taking off his socks.
现在他把袜子也脱了。

838
00:39:38.050 --> 00:39:39.110
I might move.
我可能得换个位子。

839
00:39:39.410 --> 00:39:40.310
Need snacks.
需要零食。

840
00:39:40.630 --> 00:39:41.070
BRB.
马上回来。

841
00:39:41.950 --> 00:39:44.770
Moved seats and got some type of spicy nut mix.
换了座位，还买了一种辣味坚果混合零食。

842
00:39:46.070 --> 00:39:47.310
So, family update.
那么，播报一下家庭近况。

843
00:39:47.530 --> 00:39:49.810
Josh and Kate are going to a volleyball tournament this week.
乔什和凯特这周要去参加排球锦标赛。

844
00:39:49.990 --> 00:39:52.370
Isabel and Jack are taking college courses over the summer.
伊莎贝尔和杰克暑期正在上大学课程。

845
00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:55.650
So, this is the first time I'll be taking a big trip by myself.
所以，这是我第一次独自一人进行长途旅行。

846
00:39:55.950 --> 00:39:58.390
I feel a little rusty at doing this solo.
我感觉一个人做这种事有点生疏。

847
00:39:59.570 --> 00:40:00.010
Sidebar.
顺便说一句。

848
00:40:00.150 --> 00:40:02.410
They are not playing Wimbledon in the lounge.
休息室里居然没在播温网。

849
00:40:02.930 --> 00:40:03.370
WTF.
搞什么鬼。

850
00:40:04.070 --> 00:40:07.270
There are so many TVs, but all they're showing is the World Cup.
有那么多台电视，但它们放的居然全都是世界杯。

851
00:40:07.450 --> 00:40:08.490
And look, I get it.
听着，我明白。

852
00:40:08.650 --> 00:40:08.830
Okay.
好吧。

853
00:40:09.170 --> 00:40:11.090
The World Cup is amazing and fun.
世界杯精彩又好玩。

854
00:40:11.190 --> 00:40:12.010
And I love it too.
我也很喜欢。

855
00:40:12.190 --> 00:40:15.910
But not one TV for the biggest tennis tournament of the year.
但竟然连一台播一年中最大网球赛事的电视都没有。

856
00:40:16.070 --> 00:40:16.730
Not one.
一台都没有。

857
00:40:16.730 --> 00:40:17.410
Ugh.
呃。

858
00:40:17.890 --> 00:40:18.810
Getting a glass of wine.
去倒杯葡萄酒。

859
00:40:18.950 --> 00:40:19.810
Finding out the Wi-Fi.
查一下无线网络密码。

860
00:40:19.970 --> 00:40:20.450
Please hold.
请稍候。

861
00:40:21.590 --> 00:40:22.570
That's very grumpy.
这也太暴躁了。

862
00:40:23.450 --> 00:40:23.790
Okay.
好吧。

863
00:40:23.790 --> 00:40:26.310
I'm back with wine and I'm watching Wimbledon on my laptop.
我拿好酒回来了，正用笔记本电脑看温网。

864
00:40:26.690 --> 00:40:30.810
I am trying to take a selfie of myself in the lounge with my wine and tennis on my computer
我正试着在休息室里自拍一张，把我的酒和电脑上的网球拍进去

865
00:40:30.810 --> 00:40:33.270
to send it to my mom, but I couldn't figure it out.
发给我妈，但我搞不定。

866
00:40:33.430 --> 00:40:35.890
I'm not bendy enough to fit it all in the picture.
我身体不够灵活，没办法把这些全塞进画面里。

867
00:40:36.270 --> 00:40:40.870
A very nice gentleman asked if I needed him to take the picture because I probably look so awkward.
一个非常好的绅士问我是不是需要他帮忙拍照，因为我看起来可能太别扭了。

868
00:40:41.030 --> 00:40:42.350
I'm slightly embarrassed.
我有点尴尬。

869
00:40:44.110 --> 00:40:45.150
4 p.m.
下午4点。

870
00:40:45.350 --> 00:40:48.550
British Airways flight 282 LAX to London Heathrow.
英国航空282号航班，从洛杉矶飞往伦敦希思罗。

871
00:40:49.130 --> 00:40:49.610
Okay.
好吧。

872
00:40:49.810 --> 00:40:50.910
I need to be snarky.
我得开启讽刺模式了。

873
00:40:52.330 --> 00:40:55.270
My flight attendant is 100% an Angela Martin.
我的空乘百分之百是个安吉拉·马丁。

874
00:40:55.430 --> 00:40:56.430
Severe blonde bun.
一丝不苟的金发发髻。

875
00:40:56.650 --> 00:40:57.490
So bossy.
太盛气凌人了。

876
00:40:57.650 --> 00:40:58.950
She's snippy with everyone.
她对谁都言语刻薄。

877
00:40:59.170 --> 00:41:00.590
And she's also a little gossipy.
而且她还有点八卦。

878
00:41:00.850 --> 00:41:04.890
I was in line for the bathroom and she was looking at a passenger and whispering to another flight
我当时在排队上洗手间，她正看着一个乘客，对另一个空

879
00:41:04.890 --> 00:41:06.490
attendant and then they both started laughing.
乘耳语，然后她俩都笑了起来。

880
00:41:06.890 --> 00:41:08.850
I'm trying to figure out who they're talking about.
我正琢磨她们在说谁呢。

881
00:41:09.350 --> 00:41:11.410
Maybe the man with the skeleton socks.
也许是那个穿着骷髅袜的男士。

882
00:41:11.410 --> 00:41:12.390
He does seem annoying.
他确实挺招人烦的。

883
00:41:14.950 --> 00:41:16.830
I had the beet goat cheese salad.
我吃了甜菜山羊奶酪沙拉。

884
00:41:16.970 --> 00:41:17.810
I really liked it.
我真的很喜欢。

885
00:41:18.030 --> 00:41:20.130
And then I watched the movie Midwinter Break.
然后我看了电影《寒冬假期》。

886
00:41:20.330 --> 00:41:21.010
So good.
太棒了。

887
00:41:21.270 --> 00:41:24.030
This movie deals with traumatic moments that shape us.
这部电影探讨了塑造我们人生的创伤时刻。

888
00:41:24.250 --> 00:41:28.130
Marriage ups and downs and the calling to be of greater service through our faith.
婚姻的起起落落，以及通过信仰去提供更大奉献的召唤。

889
00:41:28.350 --> 00:41:32.350
It also does a great job of showing that life happens in crowded spaces.
它同时也极好地展现了生活就发生在熙熙攘攘的空间里。

890
00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:34.950
Sadness, anger, heartbreak.
悲伤、愤怒、心碎。

891
00:41:35.150 --> 00:41:38.470
It can all happen over dinner at a restaurant with tons of people around.
这些都可能在一群人围坐的餐厅晚餐时发生。

892
00:41:38.830 --> 00:41:41.290
There is only one sex scene in this movie.
这部电影里只有一个性爱场面。

893
00:41:41.410 --> 00:41:42.270
And barely that.
而且几乎算不上。

894
00:41:42.430 --> 00:41:43.490
Like you don't see anything.
就好像你什么也看不到。

895
00:41:43.490 --> 00:41:45.070
It's just a bunch of sheets.
只有一堆床单。

896
00:41:45.390 --> 00:41:46.750
It's between two older people.
是两个老年人之间的。

897
00:41:47.010 --> 00:41:49.510
Maybe they're in their late 60s, early 70s.
也许他们六十多岁快七十，或者七十出头。

898
00:41:49.690 --> 00:41:55.530
And that is the moment when a dad from our kid's school walked up to me to say hi.
就在那个时候，我们孩子学校的一个爸爸走过来跟我打招呼。

899
00:41:56.090 --> 00:42:01.030
I paused the TV and it's two old people, barely clothed in bed together.
我暂停了电视，画面上是两个衣衫不整的老人躺在床上。

900
00:42:01.450 --> 00:42:04.030
The dad from the school said, what are you watching?
学校的那个爸爸问，你在看什么呢？

901
00:42:05.470 --> 00:42:05.990
Cringe.
真尴尬。

902
00:42:08.830 --> 00:42:10.690
July 1st, 10.30 a.m.
7月1日上午10点30分。

903
00:42:10.730 --> 00:42:12.350
I just landed at London Heathrow.
我刚在伦敦希思罗机场降落。

904
00:42:12.670 --> 00:42:14.490
It's the day after I left L.A.
这是我离开洛杉矶的第二天。

905
00:42:14.530 --> 00:42:15.790
and I barely slept on the plane.
我在飞机上几乎没怎么睡。

906
00:42:15.950 --> 00:42:17.250
I'm not sure how I'm going to stay awake.
我不知道自己要怎么保持清醒。

907
00:42:17.890 --> 00:42:21.650
In my taxi now, the driver's an older man and he said, where to, love?
我现在坐在出租车里，司机是个大叔，他问，去哪儿啊，亲爱的？

908
00:42:21.910 --> 00:42:26.290
His name is Andy and I told him my name was Angela and he said, we're the two A's.
他叫安迪，我告诉他我叫安吉拉，他说，我们俩名字都是A开头的。

909
00:42:26.530 --> 00:42:27.330
I love him.
我太喜欢他了。

910
00:42:27.950 --> 00:42:31.970
Traffic getting from the airport to my friend's flat in Highgate was really bad, but I didn't
从机场到我朋友在海格ate的公寓，交通状况非常糟糕，但我并不

911
00:42:31.970 --> 00:42:32.250
mind.
介意。

912
00:42:32.430 --> 00:42:34.590
I was tired and the taxi had air conditioning.
我很累，而且出租车有空调。

913
00:42:34.910 --> 00:42:39.250
I was almost asleep and Andy said, you might get to see the royal family.
我快睡着了，安迪说，你可能会见到皇室成员。

914
00:42:39.310 --> 00:42:40.370
So I perked up.
所以我一下子来了精神。

915
00:42:40.630 --> 00:42:44.770
On the other side of the freeway, there were a bunch of police on motorcycles clearing the
在高速公路的另一边，有一群骑摩托车的警察在为

916
00:42:44.770 --> 00:42:46.210
way for a vehicle motorcade.
一支车队开道。

917
00:42:46.410 --> 00:42:50.190
Then three big black SUVs came whizzing by.
接着三辆黑色的大型SUV呼啸而过。

918
00:42:50.670 --> 00:42:52.810
Andy said, that's one of the royals.
安迪说，那是皇室成员之一。

919
00:42:53.290 --> 00:42:57.250
And then he said, they'll never know what it's like to sit in traffic.
然后他说，他们永远不会体会到堵车是什么滋味。

920
00:42:58.490 --> 00:43:02.370
I asked him who he thought it was and he said, maybe the king.
我问他觉得那是谁，他说，也许是国王。

921
00:43:02.930 --> 00:43:07.530
Andy said, the king goes back and forth to London and then to Highgrove so he can, quote,
安迪说，国王在伦敦和海格罗夫之间往返，这样他就可以，引述原话，

922
00:43:07.930 --> 00:43:08.950
smell his flowers.
闻闻他的花香。

923
00:43:09.590 --> 00:43:11.770
I feel like Andy was throwing subtle shade.
我觉得安迪刚才在暗暗吐槽。

924
00:43:12.170 --> 00:43:13.530
Andy and I might be related.
我和安迪说不定有亲戚关系。

925
00:43:14.890 --> 00:43:17.170
July 2nd, I'm staying at my friend's in Highgate.
7月2日，我住在海格特的朋友家。

926
00:43:17.290 --> 00:43:18.810
We walked a ton yesterday.
我们昨天走了超多的路。

927
00:43:19.150 --> 00:43:22.970
My friend Betsy says that is the best way to stay awake and fight off jet lag.
我的朋友贝茜说，那是保持清醒和克服时差的最佳方法。

928
00:43:23.490 --> 00:43:26.330
Step count, I can't remember, but it was over 17,000.
步数记不清了，但超过了17,000步。

929
00:43:26.870 --> 00:43:30.750
Today, we took the tube to Marleybone to meet up with Betsy's friends, Louise and Marina
今天，我们坐地铁去马里波恩，和贝茜的朋友路易丝和玛丽娜会合，

930
00:43:30.750 --> 00:43:32.470
for what they call fancy lunch.
去吃她们所谓的高级午餐。

931
00:43:32.990 --> 00:43:34.850
So here's what you do for fancy lunch.
所以高级午餐的流程是这样的。

932
00:43:35.050 --> 00:43:36.670
First, you meet for tea and biscuits.
首先，你们见面喝茶吃饼干。

933
00:43:36.770 --> 00:43:39.510
Then you do some shopping and then you have a fancy lunch.
然后逛一会儿街，接着吃高级午餐。

934
00:43:40.250 --> 00:43:41.430
It was fantastic.
太棒了。

935
00:43:41.450 --> 00:43:42.430
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

936
00:43:43.190 --> 00:43:45.990
Then we went back to Highgate to play tennis at the park.
然后我们回海格特去公园打网球。

937
00:43:46.250 --> 00:43:49.670
Yes, you guys, I brought my racket all the way to London.
是的，各位，我把球拍一路带到了伦敦。

938
00:43:50.230 --> 00:43:53.110
Step count today was crazy, around 19,000.
今天的步数太疯狂了，大约19,000步。

939
00:43:53.110 --> 00:43:56.330
July 3rd, I have now played tennis twice in London.
7月3日，我现在已经在伦敦打过两次网球了。

940
00:43:56.530 --> 00:43:58.290
I think I'm ready for Wimbledon.
我觉得我已经准备好参加温网了。

941
00:43:58.670 --> 00:43:59.250
Ha ha.
哈哈。

942
00:44:00.030 --> 00:44:01.230
More walking today.
今天继续走路。

943
00:44:01.530 --> 00:44:02.910
Things I took pictures of.
我拍了照的东西。

944
00:44:03.070 --> 00:44:07.390
Flowers by the street, lots of hanging flowers, window box flowers, and hydrangeas.
街边的花，许多垂吊的花、窗台花箱的花，还有绣球花。

945
00:44:07.570 --> 00:44:08.510
So beautiful.
太美了。

946
00:44:08.970 --> 00:44:12.370
Also, I took pictures of ivy that grows on the sides of buildings.
我还拍了爬满建筑物侧面的常春藤。

947
00:44:13.110 --> 00:44:17.230
I am driving my friends nuts because I keep stopping to take pictures of flowers.
我快把朋友们逼疯了，因为我总是停下来拍花。

948
00:44:17.850 --> 00:44:21.470
Last night, we walked through a park and Mumford & Sons was playing a concert.
昨晚，我们穿过一个公园，蒙福乐队正在那里开演唱会。

949
00:44:21.810 --> 00:44:25.410
There was a giant fence and we could hear them from the other side.
那里有一道巨大的栅栏，我们在另一边能听到他们的歌声。

950
00:44:25.650 --> 00:44:29.290
There were a lot of people that I guess didn't get tickets or were just enjoying the concert
有很多人我想是没有买到票，或者只是在享受演唱会

951
00:44:29.290 --> 00:44:32.030
from outside on the lawn, having wine and picnics.
在外面草坪上喝红酒、野餐。

952
00:44:32.170 --> 00:44:34.590
We hung out there for a bit and heard the end of the concert.
我们在那儿闲逛了一会儿，听完了音乐会的结尾。

953
00:44:34.810 --> 00:44:35.710
It was a lovely night.
这是一个美好的夜晚。

954
00:44:36.150 --> 00:44:37.770
Step count was around 20,000.
步数大约是两万步。

955
00:44:40.290 --> 00:44:43.290
July 4th, all my tennis gals have now arrived.
7月4日，我所有的网球姐妹现在都到了。

956
00:44:43.510 --> 00:44:45.430
The four of us will be going to Wimbledon together.
我们四个人将一起去温布尔登。

957
00:44:45.930 --> 00:44:50.910
I saw a reel on Instagram that says every group of four friends on a trip has a navigator,
我在Instagram上看到一个视频，上面说旅行中的每四个朋友里，有一个是导航担当、

958
00:44:51.030 --> 00:44:53.350
a planner, and two that don't know anything.
一个规划担当，还有两个什么都不知道的。

959
00:44:54.190 --> 00:44:56.510
Well, I think for us, Betsy is the planner.
嗯，我觉得对我们来说，贝茜是规划担当。

960
00:44:56.830 --> 00:45:00.790
Rebecca actually likes to navigate and figure out all the trains and routes.
丽贝卡其实很喜欢导航，研究所有的列车和路线。

961
00:45:00.950 --> 00:45:02.650
She told me she enjoys it.
她告诉我她很享受这个。

962
00:45:02.950 --> 00:45:04.390
Thank God, because I hate it.
谢天谢地，因为我讨厌这个。

963
00:45:04.950 --> 00:45:08.090
Julie is the responsible one who makes sure we all have the things we need.
朱莉是那个负责任的人，她确保我们带齐了需要的所有东西。

964
00:45:08.210 --> 00:45:09.830
And I am the historian.
而我是历史记录员。

965
00:45:10.150 --> 00:45:14.430
I take all the pictures and document the trip and sometimes drive everyone crazy in the process.
我拍下所有的照片，记录这次旅行，有时在这个过程中把大家折腾得够呛。

966
00:45:14.430 --> 00:45:17.530
But they're always happy after the fact to have the pictures.
但事后她们总是很高兴能有这些照片。

967
00:45:17.970 --> 00:45:19.610
And you guys know I'm going to scrapbook.
而且你们知道我要做手账的。

968
00:45:19.790 --> 00:45:20.210
Yes.
是的。

969
00:45:20.430 --> 00:45:24.290
My next entry is, we are now at an Airbnb near Marble Arch.
我的下一篇日记是，我们现在在靠进大理石拱门的爱彼迎。

970
00:45:24.590 --> 00:45:29.090
This morning, we were walking to the tube station near us and there was a big truck going down the
今天早上，我们正走向附近的地铁站，有一辆大卡车开过

971
00:45:29.090 --> 00:45:33.710
street and a man was leaning out of the back of it with a special type of water hose.
街道，一个男人从车厢后探出半个身子，拿着一种特殊的水管。

972
00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:38.250
It looked like a long pole, but then it had a bend at the end and a nozzle.
它看起来像一根长竿，但末端有个弯曲处和一个喷嘴。

973
00:45:38.630 --> 00:45:42.330
He was using it to water the flower pots that hang from the lampposts.
他正用它给挂在路灯柱上的花盆浇水。

974
00:45:42.350 --> 00:45:46.410
I cannot tell you how happy that made me to see them being watered and cared for.
我无法形容看到它们被浇水和照料时我有多高兴。

975
00:45:47.630 --> 00:45:49.910
I bet you could guess it, but I took a picture.
我敢说你能猜到，我拍了张照片。

976
00:45:51.930 --> 00:45:52.750
1 p.m.
下午1点。

977
00:45:52.870 --> 00:45:56.790
Walked through a beautiful park today and there was a cafe where you could get snacks, ice cream,
今天穿过了一个美丽的公园，那里有一家咖啡馆，可以买到零食、冰淇淋，

978
00:45:56.830 --> 00:45:58.250
and also buy plants.
还可以买植物。

979
00:45:58.610 --> 00:45:59.610
I am in heaven.
我置身于天堂。

980
00:45:59.610 --> 00:46:02.010
I took a picture of the sign, Pavilion Cafe.
我拍下了那个招牌的照片，馆咖啡厅。

981
00:46:02.330 --> 00:46:05.290
And then as we walked through the park, there was a game of cricket going on.
然后当我们穿过公园时，正进行着一场板球比赛。

982
00:46:05.330 --> 00:46:07.610
So we sat on a bench and watched for a while.
于是我们坐在长椅上看了一会儿。

983
00:46:07.790 --> 00:46:10.570
I also fell in love with a floppy Datsun named Peanut.
我还爱上了一只叫“花生”的垂耳腊肠犬。

984
00:46:10.910 --> 00:46:12.830
I would love a floppy Datsun.
我也好想要一只垂耳腊肠犬。

985
00:46:12.990 --> 00:46:15.510
I love any type of dog that looks like a big burrito.
我喜欢任何长得像大卷饼的狗。

986
00:46:16.630 --> 00:46:17.470
3 p.m.
下午3点。

987
00:46:17.570 --> 00:46:18.890
Went to the department store Liberty.
去了利宝百货。

988
00:46:18.910 --> 00:46:20.010
It's so beautiful.
它太漂亮了。

989
00:46:20.330 --> 00:46:22.370
It was founded in 1875.
它始建于1875年。

990
00:46:22.470 --> 00:46:25.330
It's several floors tall in an old Tudor style building.
它有好多层高，是一座古老的都铎风格建筑。

991
00:46:25.570 --> 00:46:28.050
I love the wooden staircase and the ceiling.
我喜欢木质楼梯和天花板。

992
00:46:28.050 --> 00:46:30.970
I bought a cute summer robe with a navy floral design.
我买了一件带海军蓝碎花设计的可爱夏日长袍。

993
00:46:31.270 --> 00:46:32.710
Step count today was crazy.
今天的步数太疯狂了。

994
00:46:32.990 --> 00:46:34.770
23,102.
23,102步。

995
00:46:35.030 --> 00:46:37.570
My watch says I climbed 25 flights of stairs.
我的手表显示我爬了25层楼。

996
00:46:38.210 --> 00:46:38.690
Wow.
哇。

997
00:46:38.970 --> 00:46:39.450
I know.
我知道。

998
00:46:39.790 --> 00:46:41.450
You haven't even gotten to Wimbledon yet.
你们甚至还没去温布尔登呢。

999
00:46:41.450 --> 00:46:41.870
I know.
我知道。

1000
00:46:41.990 --> 00:46:42.690
I have one day.
我还有一天时间。

1001
00:46:42.830 --> 00:46:44.350
I forgot that's where this is headed.
我忘了事情会发展到这一步。

1002
00:46:46.530 --> 00:46:48.430
July 5th, 11 p.m.
7月5日，晚上11点。

1003
00:46:48.830 --> 00:46:49.750
So tired.
好累。

1004
00:46:49.750 --> 00:46:51.670
But I wanted to jot down about my day.
但我想把今天的事情记下来。

1005
00:46:51.890 --> 00:46:55.050
I bought a tin full of tea with Queen Elizabeth's face on it.
我买了一罐印有伊丽莎白女王头像的茶。

1006
00:46:55.050 --> 00:46:59.490
There were a bunch of different royal family members' faces on tins of tea to choose from.
有好多不同王室成员头像的茶罐可以选。

1007
00:46:59.630 --> 00:47:00.910
But I went with Queen Elizabeth.
但我选了伊丽莎白女王。

1008
00:47:01.390 --> 00:47:03.210
I also bought a cute tote bag for Isabel.
我还给伊莎贝尔买了一个可爱的托特包。

1009
00:47:03.490 --> 00:47:04.590
And a Christmas ornament.
还有一个圣诞装饰品。

1010
00:47:04.810 --> 00:47:07.450
I always buy an ornament from our travels and the kids love it.
我每次旅行都会买一个装饰品，孩子们都很喜欢。

1011
00:47:07.550 --> 00:47:11.090
So this year we'll be adding a little figurine of Paddington the Bear to the tree.
所以今年我们的圣诞树上会多出一个帕丁顿熊的小塑像。

1012
00:47:11.510 --> 00:47:15.250
Oh, and I also went to see the play adaptation of My Neighbor Totoro.
哦，对了，我还去看了话剧版的《龙猫》。

1013
00:47:15.590 --> 00:47:16.230
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1014
00:47:16.490 --> 00:47:19.550
I teared about the end when the cast and puppeteers took their bow.
当演员和木偶师谢幕时，看到结尾我都快哭了。

1015
00:47:19.730 --> 00:47:21.770
We all stood on our feet and applauded them.
我们全都起立为他们鼓掌。

1016
00:47:21.770 --> 00:47:25.090
And it's what I love about theater or making TV or film.
这也是我热爱戏剧、电视或电影的原因。

1017
00:47:25.310 --> 00:47:28.750
So many people behind the scenes that come together to make a piece of art.
幕后有那么多人齐心协力创作出了一件艺术品。

1018
00:47:28.990 --> 00:47:29.710
It's truly moving.
真的很感人。

1019
00:47:31.250 --> 00:47:33.010
July 6th, 8 a.m.
7月6日，早上8点。

1020
00:47:33.350 --> 00:47:35.530
Drinking my tea and steaming my dress.
喝着茶，用挂烫机烫我的裙子。

1021
00:47:35.730 --> 00:47:38.390
Today I feel like that moment when Michael Scott was screaming,
今天我的感觉就像迈克尔·斯科特大喊的那一幕一样，

1022
00:47:38.610 --> 00:47:40.290
Oh my God, it's happening!
天哪，要发生啦！

1023
00:47:40.870 --> 00:47:42.250
Today is Wimbledon!
今天是温网！

1024
00:47:42.450 --> 00:47:42.930
Ah!
啊！

1025
00:47:43.390 --> 00:47:44.550
I'm so excited!
我太兴奋了！

1026
00:47:44.830 --> 00:47:45.590
No time to journal.
没时间写日记了。

1027
00:47:45.690 --> 00:47:46.230
Must get ready.
得去准备了。

1028
00:47:46.430 --> 00:47:49.230
Also, my travel steamer is fantastic and tiny and folds up.
另外，我的旅行挂烫机太棒了，又小又能折叠。

1029
00:47:49.330 --> 00:47:50.630
It's by a company called Next Do.
是叫Next Do的公司的产品。

1030
00:47:50.630 --> 00:47:52.290
Okay, I felt like that was important to share.
好吧，我觉得分享这个很重要。

1031
00:47:52.750 --> 00:47:54.670
Okay, July 7th.
好吧，7月7日。

1032
00:47:55.370 --> 00:47:56.110
Good morning.
早安。

1033
00:47:56.530 --> 00:47:57.550
I woke up early.
我醒得很早。

1034
00:47:57.770 --> 00:47:58.650
I couldn't sleep.
我睡不着。

1035
00:47:58.990 --> 00:48:01.070
I stayed up late with the time difference,
由于时差，我熬得很晚，

1036
00:48:01.250 --> 00:48:05.290
talking to my mom to tell her every detail of my day at Wimbledon.
跟我妈聊天，把我在温网这一天的每个细节都告诉了她。

1037
00:48:05.610 --> 00:48:07.050
She was thrilled.
她听得兴奋极了。

1038
00:48:07.730 --> 00:48:10.170
Yesterday was one of the best days of my life.
昨天是我人生中最美好的日子之一。

1039
00:48:10.310 --> 00:48:11.690
I don't even know where to begin.
我都不知道该从何说起。

1040
00:48:11.990 --> 00:48:16.210
I took a ton of pictures and jotted things down in my notes app so I could share in my journal.
我拍了大量的照片，并在便签应用里记下了事情，这样我就可以在日记里分享了。

1041
00:48:16.730 --> 00:48:18.050
Let's start with my outfit.
先从我的穿搭说起吧。

1042
00:48:18.330 --> 00:48:18.810
Fit check.
穿搭检查。

1043
00:48:18.810 --> 00:48:24.110
I wore a green linen dress by Bowdoin and comfy white sneakers with a green trim by Viva.
我穿了一条Bowdoin的绿色亚麻连衣裙，还搭配了一双带绿色滚边的舒适小白鞋，牌子是Viva。

1044
00:48:24.430 --> 00:48:25.650
I don't know how to say it.
我不知道这个词怎么读。

1045
00:48:25.890 --> 00:48:30.570
And then I also brought a tote bag with an empty water bottle because you can refill it once you get inside.
然后我还带了一个托特包和一个空水瓶，因为进到里面后你可以重新灌满水。

1046
00:48:30.730 --> 00:48:31.770
Sunscreen and a hat.
防晒霜和一顶帽子。

1047
00:48:32.250 --> 00:48:32.930
Very important.
非常重要。

1048
00:48:33.550 --> 00:48:34.570
9.30 a.m.
上午9点30分。

1049
00:48:34.570 --> 00:48:38.210
We left early to grab some breakfast to go, or as they say here, to take away.
我们早早出发去买点外带早餐，或者像这里的人说的那样，带走吃。

1050
00:48:38.470 --> 00:48:41.110
And then we took the train from Marble Arch to Wimbledon.
然后我们坐火车从大理石拱门出发前往温布尔登。

1051
00:48:41.390 --> 00:48:46.050
Thank you to the folks we met at a coffee shop who told us to get off at Southfield Station.
感谢我们在咖啡馆遇到的人，他们告诉我们在南菲尔德站下车。

1052
00:48:46.370 --> 00:48:49.010
If you guys ever go and take the tube, get off there.
如果你们以后去坐伦敦地铁，就在那里下车。

1053
00:48:49.350 --> 00:48:52.930
Then you walk to the entrance gates of Wimbledon, and it's not a bad walk.
然后步行到温网的入口大门，这段路走起来并不算太累。

1054
00:48:53.030 --> 00:48:54.010
About 15 minutes.
大约15分钟。

1055
00:48:54.010 --> 00:48:57.130
The whole walk to the gates, I had a body buzz.
一路上走到大门时，我整个人都兴奋得微颤。

1056
00:48:57.430 --> 00:48:59.550
You could feel a joy in the crowd we walked with.
你能从和我们同行的人群中感受到一种喜悦。

1057
00:48:59.710 --> 00:49:04.890
A huge group of strangers, all dressed in what looked like their Sunday best, excited for the day ahead.
一大群素不相识的人，都穿着看起来像他们最好看的衣服，对即将到来的一天充满期待。

1058
00:49:05.290 --> 00:49:09.310
10.30 a.m., walking into the courts, we had four tickets.
上午10点30分，走进球场时，我们有四张票。

1059
00:49:09.530 --> 00:49:11.630
Two to center court and two to court one.
两张是中心球场的，两张是一号球场的。

1060
00:49:11.910 --> 00:49:14.750
Throughout the day, we would trade seats so we could see different matches.
一整天下来，我们会交换座位，这样就能看不同的比赛。

1061
00:49:15.050 --> 00:49:17.370
The first match I saw was on center court.
我看的首场比赛是在中心球场。

1062
00:49:17.610 --> 00:49:20.550
Walking into that stadium felt like a religious experience.
走进那个体育场感觉就像经历了一场宗教仪式。

1063
00:49:20.910 --> 00:49:26.830
Our seats were across from the royal box, so I had a great view of Roger Federer and Billie Jean King.
我们的座位正对着皇家包厢，所以我把罗杰·费德勒和比利·简·金看得清清楚楚。

1064
00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:27.690
OMG!
天哪！

1065
00:49:28.370 --> 00:49:29.850
The match was amazing.
这场比赛太精彩了。

1066
00:49:30.010 --> 00:49:33.650
It was Jasmine Paulini and Alexandra Iala, and they absolutely floored me.
是贾丝米妮·保利尼对阵亚历山德拉·埃亚拉，她们彻底把我惊艳到了。

1067
00:49:33.650 --> 00:49:39.450
We had two very charming men from Italy sitting behind us, and whenever Paulini hit a winner, they would chant,
我们身后坐着两个来自意大利的迷人男士，每当保利尼打出制胜分，他们就会高喊：

1068
00:49:40.590 --> 00:49:40.990
Bravissimo!
太棒了！

1069
00:49:40.990 --> 00:49:41.390
Bravissimo!
太棒了！

1070
00:49:41.930 --> 00:49:44.350
It's such good people watching at Wimbledon, too.
在温网看形形色色的人也是一大乐趣。

1071
00:49:44.510 --> 00:49:49.670
I met a woman named Jude who had a hat covered in tennis balls, but somehow it was also fashionable.
我遇到了一位名叫朱德的女士，她戴着一顶贴满网球的帽子，但不知怎么的，还挺时髦的。

1072
00:49:50.070 --> 00:49:53.290
I asked her where she got it, and she told me she made it.
我问她是在哪买的，她告诉我是自己做的。

1073
00:49:53.770 --> 00:49:55.550
She said, all you need is a glue gun.
她说，你只需要一把热熔胶枪。

1074
00:49:55.890 --> 00:49:57.090
I got very excited.
我变得非常兴奋。

1075
00:49:57.090 --> 00:49:59.810
I have a glue gun, and I want to make one.
我有一把热熔胶枪，我也想做一个。

1076
00:50:00.050 --> 00:50:00.850
Oh, dear.
哦，天哪。

1077
00:50:01.110 --> 00:50:03.350
And she let me take a picture, lady, of her hat.
而且她让我拍了张照片，那位女士，拍了她的帽子。

1078
00:50:03.350 --> 00:50:04.830
And I really want to try to make it.
我真的很想尝试做一个。

1079
00:50:05.030 --> 00:50:07.670
Will I be the crazy lady wearing a hat with tennis balls?
我会不会变成那个戴着粘满网球的帽子的疯狂女人？

1080
00:50:07.910 --> 00:50:08.150
Yeah.
会吧。

1081
00:50:08.450 --> 00:50:08.630
Maybe.
也许会。

1082
00:50:08.990 --> 00:50:09.170
Okay.
好吧。

1083
00:50:09.710 --> 00:50:10.630
Back to my journal.
回到我的日记。

1084
00:50:11.390 --> 00:50:13.550
Throughout the day, there were so many fantastic matches.
这一天里，有太多精彩绝伦的比赛了。

1085
00:50:13.550 --> 00:50:15.790
I felt humbled to be there and spent the day in awe.
能去到那里让我感到很荣幸，一整天都处于惊叹之中。

1086
00:50:16.110 --> 00:50:17.490
There was a moment I won't forget.
有一个时刻我永远不会忘记。

1087
00:50:17.670 --> 00:50:20.230
It was in the Arthur Ferry and Grigor Dimitrov match.
那是在阿瑟·费瑞和格里戈尔·季米特洛夫的比赛中。

1088
00:50:20.690 --> 00:50:23.110
Ferry won the wild card slot to play.
费瑞赢得了外卡名额得以参赛。

1089
00:50:23.590 --> 00:50:27.810
This means he didn't have a high enough ranking to normally get a chance to compete.
这意味着他的排名不够高，通常没有机会参赛。

1090
00:50:28.050 --> 00:50:29.570
He wouldn't have even been there.
他本甚至不会出现在那里。

1091
00:50:29.570 --> 00:50:31.530
But he got the wild card.
但他获得了外卡。

1092
00:50:31.730 --> 00:50:35.950
And Dimitrov has been on the professional tennis circuit around 18 years.
而季米特洛夫在职业网球巡回赛上大约已经有18年了。

1093
00:50:36.290 --> 00:50:40.030
The energy in that stadium was absolutely electric.
那个体育场里的气氛简直热烈爆棚。

1094
00:50:40.450 --> 00:50:45.950
They played amazing tennis and went five sets that led then to an insane tiebreaker.
他们打出了精彩的网球，打满了五盘，随后迎来了一场疯狂的抢七。

1095
00:50:46.870 --> 00:50:48.710
Ferry is from the Wimbledon area.
费瑞是温网本地人。

1096
00:50:48.710 --> 00:50:52.970
And at one point when the stadium was very quiet, a fan yelled,
有一次，当体育场非常安静时，一个球迷大喊：

1097
00:50:53.230 --> 00:50:54.510
Go on, Ferry!
加油，费瑞！

1098
00:50:54.930 --> 00:50:56.870
And the place went nuts.
然后全场都疯狂了。

1099
00:50:57.190 --> 00:50:59.490
This match could have easily gone either way.
这场比赛鹿死谁手真的很难说。

1100
00:50:59.650 --> 00:51:02.170
But in the end, Ferry won.
但最终，费瑞赢了。

1101
00:51:02.170 --> 00:51:04.890
And the place went berserk.
整个场面瞬间沸腾了。

1102
00:51:05.390 --> 00:51:10.890
Here's this local kid with a wild card now going to the quarterfinals at Wimbledon.
这是一个当地的小将，手握外卡，如今闯入了温网的四分之一决赛。

1103
00:51:11.050 --> 00:51:15.310
You felt the weight of that moment wash over him and he dropped to the ground.
你能感受到那一刻的重压向他袭来，他倒在了地上。

1104
00:51:15.590 --> 00:51:18.610
I had to wipe away some tears and I wasn't the only one.
我忍不住擦拭泪水，而且流泪的不止我一个。

1105
00:51:18.610 --> 00:51:22.990
I looked around that packed stadium and people were crying, hugging, and cheering.
我环顾那个座无虚席的球场，人们在哭泣、拥抱和欢呼。

1106
00:51:23.330 --> 00:51:26.970
It made me think of our discussion with Mike Schur about fandom.
这让我想起了我们与迈克·舒尔关于粉丝文化的讨论。

1107
00:51:27.310 --> 00:51:31.830
This one singular moment brought a crowd of strangers together in pure joy.
这独一无二的瞬间将一群陌生人紧紧联系在一起，洋溢着纯粹的喜悦。

1108
00:51:32.150 --> 00:51:34.330
And the food and drink of it all.
还有那里的各种美食和饮品。

1109
00:51:34.670 --> 00:51:38.090
Yes, I needed to know if you had strawberries and Pimm's.
没错，我得知道你们有没有吃草莓和喝Pimm's酒。

1110
00:51:38.350 --> 00:51:41.130
Yes, I had strawberries and cream and a Pimm's.
是的，我吃了奶油草莓，还喝了Pimm's酒。

1111
00:51:41.290 --> 00:51:43.710
And I got to go into the Wimbledon broadcast building.
我甚至有机会参观了温网的转播大楼。

1112
00:51:43.710 --> 00:51:50.270
I hopped on the Access All England show, which is a behind-the-scenes live stream on the Wimbledon
我上了《Access All England》节目，这是温网

1113
00:51:50.270 --> 00:51:55.290
app with my dear friend Nick McCarvel and his co-host and former professional tennis player
官方App上的一个幕后直播节目，和我亲爱的朋友尼克·麦卡维尔以及他的联合主持、前职业网球运动员

1114
00:51:55.290 --> 00:51:56.470
Jill Krabus.
吉尔·克拉布斯一起。

1115
00:51:57.170 --> 00:51:59.010
Shout out to everyone in the broadcast building.
向转播大楼里的所有人致敬。

1116
00:51:59.010 --> 00:52:03.770
They let me keep my giant bag of merch there all day so I didn't have to carry it around.
他们让我把一大袋周边商品寄存在那里一整天，这样我就不用到处拎着了。

1117
00:52:04.210 --> 00:52:08.930
I think I bought everything they make in the Wimbledon shop because, you know,
我想我把温网商店里所有的产品都买下来了，因为你知道的，

1118
00:52:08.930 --> 00:52:10.110
I love the merch!
我太爱买周边了！

1119
00:52:10.550 --> 00:52:11.250
Exclamation point.
感叹号。

1120
00:52:11.710 --> 00:52:16.350
And I have to share a lovely text I got that night from Beth in the broadcast building.
我必须分享一条当晚我收到的来自转播大楼贝丝的可爱短信。

1121
00:52:16.490 --> 00:52:17.310
She said,
她说：

1122
00:52:17.850 --> 00:52:21.910
We're here super late, so let me know whenever you're looking to grab your bits and bobs.
我们还要在这待到很晚，所以你什么时候想来拿你的零碎东西随时告诉我。

1123
00:52:22.070 --> 00:52:24.530
Do you want me to bring you guys some snacks or anything?
要我给你们带点零食什么的吗？

1124
00:52:25.150 --> 00:52:27.290
Crisps or chocolate for the journey back?
回程路上吃的薯片或巧克力？

1125
00:52:28.110 --> 00:52:29.530
We were starving.
我们当时饿坏了。

1126
00:52:29.830 --> 00:52:31.750
All the food vendors had closed by that time.
那个时候所有的食品摊都关门了。

1127
00:52:31.970 --> 00:52:33.450
So Beth, thank you for the snacks.
所以贝丝，谢谢你的零食。

1128
00:52:33.490 --> 00:52:34.730
We ate it on the way home.
我们在回家的路上把它吃光了。

1129
00:52:35.030 --> 00:52:37.470
I have a video from the end of the day of us,
我有一段我们一天结束时的视频，

1130
00:52:37.470 --> 00:52:39.470
and we literally closed the place down.
我们真的是待到这里关门才走。

1131
00:52:39.670 --> 00:52:41.410
We were there over 12 hours.
我们在那呆了12个多小时。

1132
00:52:41.710 --> 00:52:44.450
I didn't want to leave, and I hope someday I get to go back.
我真舍不得离开，希望有一天我还能再来。

1133
00:52:45.270 --> 00:52:45.750
Alrighty.
好啦。

1134
00:52:46.050 --> 00:52:50.350
I've had my Queen Elizabeth tea, and now it's time for my very last day here.
我已经喝过伊丽莎白女王茶，现在是在这里的最后一天了。

1135
00:52:50.490 --> 00:52:52.550
We're going to Notting Hill and Richmond.
我们要去诺丁山和里士满。

1136
00:52:53.410 --> 00:52:55.030
And then I have my last day.
然后就是我的最后一天。

1137
00:52:55.550 --> 00:52:58.170
Okay, last day in London, July 8th.
好的，在伦敦的最后一天，7月8日。

1138
00:52:58.550 --> 00:53:00.210
Hi from the London Heathrow Airport.
伦敦希思罗机场发来问候。

1139
00:53:00.530 --> 00:53:01.730
Today I go back home.
今天要回家了。

1140
00:53:02.010 --> 00:53:04.610
I miss my family, and I'm ready for my bed.
我想念家人，也渴望回到自己的床上。

1141
00:53:04.750 --> 00:53:06.710
But oh my goodness, do I love London.
但是天哪，我是多么热爱伦敦啊。

1142
00:53:07.170 --> 00:53:08.730
Yesterday we went to Notting Hill.
昨天我们去了诺丁山。

1143
00:53:08.990 --> 00:53:10.630
It's as charming as I could have imagined.
它比我想象的还要迷人。

1144
00:53:10.870 --> 00:53:14.870
I loved all the buildings painted different colors and all the different shops.
我喜欢所有涂成不同颜色的建筑和琳琅满目的店铺。

1145
00:53:15.110 --> 00:53:16.530
Here's something to know about me.
有些关于我的事你得知道。

1146
00:53:17.410 --> 00:53:19.690
Again, my journal who doesn't know me, I guess.
话说回来，我的日记本可能还不认识我吧，我想。

1147
00:53:19.710 --> 00:53:20.250
Never met you.
从没见过你呢。

1148
00:53:20.470 --> 00:53:20.590
Yeah.
是的。

1149
00:53:20.810 --> 00:53:22.070
Here's something to know about me.
有些关于我的事你得知道。

1150
00:53:22.170 --> 00:53:22.890
I love maps.
我喜欢地图。

1151
00:53:23.030 --> 00:53:24.470
I'm kind of obsessed with maps.
我有点痴迷于地图。

1152
00:53:24.710 --> 00:53:27.110
I have two different maps hanging as art in my house.
我家挂着两张不同的地图作为装饰画。

1153
00:53:27.330 --> 00:53:29.490
And for my folks who also like maps,
对于同样喜欢地图的朋友们，

1154
00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:32.430
there is a fantastic vintage map store in Notting Hill.
诺丁山有一家非常棒的复古地图店。

1155
00:53:32.430 --> 00:53:34.790
The Portobello Print and Map Shop.
波多贝罗版画与地图店。

1156
00:53:35.090 --> 00:53:36.610
Listen to what all they have.
听听他们都有什么。

1157
00:53:36.790 --> 00:53:41.590
Old maps, engravings, plus decorative flower, animal, and maritime prints.
旧地图、雕刻版画，还有装饰性的花卉、动物和航海版画。

1158
00:53:41.790 --> 00:53:42.930
Um, yes, please.
嗯，太好了，来一份。

1159
00:53:43.470 --> 00:53:46.430
I really wanted this big map, but I knew I couldn't fit it in my suitcase.
我真的很想要这张大地图，但我知道我的行李箱装不下。

1160
00:53:46.590 --> 00:53:50.650
So instead, I got this amazing antique engraving dated 1683.
所以我买了这个1683年的惊艳古董雕刻版画。

1161
00:53:51.210 --> 00:53:55.230
It's of the port in Cartagena with all the old-timey boats pulling in.
