00:58:59.250 --> 00:59:00.710
It's Sam and I'm in Canada,
我是山姆，我在加拿大，

1339
00:59:01.070 --> 00:59:03.030
the land of Celine Dion and Poutine.
席琳·迪翁和肉汁奶酪薯条的故乡。

1340
00:59:03.710 --> 00:59:07.650
Myself and Stephanie are on our way through her parents' house to take a van together to the airport.
我和斯蒂芬妮正在去她父母家的路上，准备一起坐面包车去机场。

1341
00:59:07.930 --> 00:59:10.370
I'm aware this is exactly how Home Alone starts.
我知道这正是《小鬼当家》的开头方式。

1342
00:59:10.510 --> 00:59:12.870
So I'll be counting everyone before we get in the van.
所以我上车前会清点每个人的头数。

1343
00:59:13.530 --> 00:59:15.850
Steph's parents really highlight the difference in our travel.
斯蒂芬的父母真切地突显了我们旅行方式的不同。

1344
00:59:15.850 --> 00:59:16.950
Or more accurately,
或者更准确地说，

1345
00:59:17.230 --> 00:59:19.890
they highlight the poor boxcar hobo way I've traveled.
他们突显了我那种寒酸流浪汉式的旅行方式。

1346
00:59:20.170 --> 00:59:20.790
For instance,
比如，

1347
00:59:20.970 --> 00:59:23.170
her dad was insistent I get travel insurance.
她爸爸坚持让我买旅游保险。

1348
00:59:23.370 --> 00:59:25.430
What the f*** is travel insurance?
他妈的什么叫旅游保险？

1349
00:59:25.950 --> 00:59:28.670
Steph asked me what I would do if I got hurt in another country.
斯蒂芬问我如果在另一个国家受伤了会怎么做。

1350
00:59:28.870 --> 00:59:31.210
I thought about it and realized as a proud American,
我思考了一下，意识到作为一个骄傲的美国人，

1351
00:59:31.210 --> 00:59:33.510
my plan was if I ever got hurt in another country.
我的计划是，如果我在另一个国家受伤，

1352
00:59:33.770 --> 00:59:35.270
I would simply die there.
我就直接死在那里。

1353
00:59:35.490 --> 00:59:39.970
They would put my hat on a poorly made cross on the spot where they buried me like an Oregon trail.
他们会把我的帽子挂在一个粗制滥造的十字架上，插在我被埋葬的地方，就像《俄勒冈小径》里那样。

1354
00:59:40.610 --> 00:59:41.510
3 p.m.
下午3点。

1355
00:59:41.650 --> 00:59:42.770
We arrived at the airport.
我们到达了机场。

1356
00:59:43.070 --> 00:59:48.010
Steph's pre-flight anxiety is again highlighting my complete lack of interior flight sense.
斯蒂芬的行前焦虑再次凸显了我对内在航班方向感的完全缺乏。

1357
00:59:48.250 --> 00:59:50.690
She travels much how I imagined Jenna would fly,
她旅行的方式很像我脑海中杰娜会坐飞机的方式，

1358
00:59:50.850 --> 00:59:54.690
with her travel documentation in an alphabetical binder by her side,
身旁放着按字母顺序排列好的旅行证件文件夹，

1359
00:59:54.830 --> 00:59:57.610
whereas I travel how I imagine Angela travels.
而我旅行的方式就像我想象中安吉拉旅行的方式一样。

1360
00:59:57.810 --> 00:59:59.830
My passport loose in my backpack,
我的护照随便塞在双肩包里，

1361
01:00:00.070 --> 01:00:02.090
stickily covered in Sour Patch Kids sugar.
上面黏糊糊地沾满了酸甜软糖的糖粉。

1362
01:00:02.550 --> 01:00:03.170
7 a.m.
早上7点。

1363
01:00:03.230 --> 01:00:03.770
the next morning,
第二天早上，

1364
01:00:03.790 --> 01:00:04.870
we have arrived in Munich.
我们已经到达了慕尼黑。

1365
01:00:05.070 --> 01:00:06.170
Our flight was eight hours,
我们的航班飞行了八个小时，

1366
01:00:06.290 --> 01:00:08.050
so we got a full meal and a breakfaSt.
所以我们吃了一顿正餐和一顿早餐。

1367
01:00:08.050 --> 01:00:10.270
Steph and her mom didn't want any yogurt,
斯蒂芬和她妈妈不想要酸奶，

1368
01:00:10.270 --> 01:00:12.750
so I got three full yogurts.
所以我得到了三整盒酸奶。

1369
01:00:12.890 --> 01:00:16.010
I know that sentence will be exciting for both Jenna and Angela.
我知道这句话会让杰娜和安吉拉都兴奋不已。

1370
01:00:16.770 --> 01:00:17.750
7.47 a.m.
早上7点47分。

1371
01:00:17.910 --> 01:00:20.470
Slight airport train to airport baggage claim.
坐了短暂的机场轻轨去取行李。

1372
01:00:20.670 --> 01:00:22.590
I am delirious with airplane sleep
我在飞机的睡眠不足中神志不清，

1373
01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:24.730
and nothing coming out of my mouth makes sense to me.
我说出的任何话自己都听不懂。

1374
01:00:24.890 --> 01:00:26.190
Nothing I need to worry about.
没什么需要担心的。

1375
01:00:26.450 --> 01:00:27.990
Not my monkey, not my circus.
不关我的事，少来烦我。

1376
01:00:28.230 --> 01:00:28.850
That's my motto.
这是我的座右铭。

1377
01:00:29.430 --> 01:00:31.810
Nicht mein Affe, nicht mein Zirkus.
Nicht mein Affe, nicht mein Zirkus。

1378
01:00:32.130 --> 01:00:32.810
10 a.m.
上午10点。

1379
01:00:32.830 --> 01:00:36.190
We are attempting to take the train from Munich airport to Steph's uncle's house.
我们正试图坐火车从慕尼黑机场去斯蒂芬叔叔家。

1380
01:00:36.190 --> 01:00:38.090
We've already gotten off on an incorrect stop
我们已经在错误的站点下过车了，

1381
01:00:38.090 --> 01:00:39.630
and then a bus no one told us to take.
还坐了一辆没人通知我们要坐的公交车。

1382
01:00:39.850 --> 01:00:40.890
We are back on the train.
我们又坐上了火车。

1383
01:00:41.030 --> 01:00:41.570
We got off.
我们下车了。

1384
01:00:41.930 --> 01:00:42.830
12.20 a.m.
中午12点20分。

1385
01:00:43.010 --> 01:00:44.930
I have now been traveling for 24 hours.
我到现在已经旅行了24个小时。

1386
01:00:45.090 --> 01:00:46.850
My passport has merged with my hands,
我的护照已经和我的手长在了一起，

1387
01:00:46.950 --> 01:00:50.030
and I am only able to say Guten Tag and Ish Heises Sam.
而且我只会说“Guten Tag”和“Ish Heises Sam”。

1388
01:00:50.170 --> 01:00:51.790
But we are at the hotel,
但我们已经到了酒店，

1389
01:00:51.830 --> 01:00:53.210
which has no AC.
这里没有空调。

1390
01:00:53.470 --> 01:00:55.630
So with Ma and her kerchief and I in my cap,
所以，带着头巾的妈妈和我戴着帽子的我，

1391
01:00:55.790 --> 01:00:58.470
I've just settled in for a 90 degree Fahrenheit,
我刚刚准备好小睡一会儿，享受华氏90度、

1392
01:00:58.730 --> 01:01:00.330
35 degree Celsius nap.
摄氏35度的室温。

1393
01:01:00.330 --> 01:01:02.150
Thanks to global warming.
多亏了全球变暖。

1394
01:01:02.530 --> 01:01:03.670
Because 60 years ago,
因为60年前，

1395
01:01:03.810 --> 01:01:06.810
a bunch of baby boomers threw a bunch of styrofoam in the foreSt.
一帮婴儿潮一代把一堆泡沫塑料扔进了森林里。

1396
01:01:06.970 --> 01:01:08.970
And now I'll never be able to afford a house
现在我永远买不起房子了，

1397
01:01:08.970 --> 01:01:10.190
and the world is on fire.
而且世界正在燃烧。

1398
01:01:10.370 --> 01:01:13.250
And I eat a credit card's worth of microplastic each week.
我每周吃掉的微塑料相当于一张信用卡的量。

1399
01:01:13.790 --> 01:01:14.090
Guten Abend.
Guten Abend。

1400
01:01:20.430 --> 01:01:22.690
So that was sent out of my mind.
所以刚才那些话我都是神志不清时说的。

1401
01:01:22.790 --> 01:01:24.570
Do you definitely get best production value?
你们绝对能做出最棒的制作效果吗？

1402
01:01:25.050 --> 01:01:25.100
Sam, you put all the music and everything.
萨姆，你负责了所有的音乐和一切。

1403
01:01:25.270 --> 01:01:26.090
That was so cool.
太酷了。

1404
01:01:26.110 --> 01:01:27.330
From my hotel room.
从我的酒店房间里。

1405
01:01:27.590 --> 01:01:28.330
No way.
不会吧。

1406
01:01:28.410 --> 01:01:28.670
Yeah.
对啊。

1407
01:01:28.910 --> 01:01:29.990
That was so cool.
太酷了。

1408
01:01:30.150 --> 01:01:31.850
What a crazy long travel day.
真是漫长又疯狂的一天旅程。

1409
01:01:31.850 --> 01:01:32.670
And here's the thing.
关键是这样的。

1410
01:01:33.010 --> 01:01:33.750
The trip itself,
这次旅行本身，

1411
01:01:33.870 --> 01:01:35.550
despite the delirium of travel,
尽管有旅途的疲惫和精神恍惚，

1412
01:01:35.650 --> 01:01:36.130
was gorgeous.
美极了。

1413
01:01:36.270 --> 01:01:37.470
I'd never been to Germany before.
我以前从未去过德国。

1414
01:01:38.030 --> 01:01:38.970
Munich was awesome.
慕尼黑太棒了。

1415
01:01:39.150 --> 01:01:40.250
We took a bullet train,
我们坐了子弹头列车，

1416
01:01:40.390 --> 01:01:42.010
which went like 250 miles an hour,
时速大概有250英里，

1417
01:01:42.190 --> 01:01:43.450
up to Osnabrück.
一直开到奥斯纳布吕克。

1418
01:01:44.010 --> 01:01:47.610
Osnabrück was built in 780 A.D.
奥斯纳布吕克建于公元780年。

1419
01:01:48.050 --> 01:01:49.810
Like that's 1,200 years ago.
就像那是1200年前一样。

1420
01:01:49.910 --> 01:01:51.450
America's like 250 years old.
美国也就250年历史。

1421
01:01:51.570 --> 01:01:51.690
Oh, I know.
哦，我知道。

1422
01:01:51.870 --> 01:01:53.970
So everything there is so old
所以那里的一切都那么古老

1423
01:01:53.970 --> 01:01:55.130
and still operational.
而且现在还在使用。

1424
01:01:55.370 --> 01:01:56.310
Like it was built well.
就好像质量很好一样。

1425
01:01:56.510 --> 01:01:58.110
And like there's a church there
而且那里有一座教堂

1426
01:01:58.110 --> 01:01:59.910
that was around since I think 800.
我想它从800年左右就存在了。

1427
01:02:00.190 --> 01:02:01.150
Just casually,
随随便便的，

1428
01:02:01.150 --> 01:02:02.150
you can just pop your head in.
你就能把头探进去看看。

1429
01:02:02.170 --> 01:02:02.810
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

1430
01:02:03.090 --> 01:02:03.570
So cool.
太酷了。

1431
01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:03.850
Yeah.
对啊。

1432
01:02:04.990 --> 01:02:05.890
Well, everyone,
好了，各位，

1433
01:02:06.050 --> 01:02:08.130
we hope you enjoyed this episode
我们希望你们喜欢这期

1434
01:02:08.130 --> 01:02:10.110
about all of our summer travels.
关于我们所有夏日旅行的节目。

1435
01:02:10.170 --> 01:02:11.630
If you have a suggestion
如果你有什么建议

1436
01:02:11.630 --> 01:02:14.870
for where you think Angela and I should go
觉得我和安吉拉应该去哪里

1437
01:02:15.490 --> 01:02:16.470
on our trip
去旅行

1438
01:02:16.470 --> 01:02:18.190
that we will then journal about,
然后我们要写进手记里的话，

1439
01:02:18.430 --> 01:02:19.510
will you please write us?
请写信给我们好吗？

1440
01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:20.950
We have a new folder at
我们在 officeladies.com

1441
01:02:20.950 --> 01:02:22.950
officeladies.com for general mail.
设立了一个新的通用邮件文件夹。

1442
01:02:23.150 --> 01:02:24.530
So tell us in the general mailbox
所以请在通用邮箱里告诉我们

1443
01:02:24.530 --> 01:02:26.790
where you think Angela and I should go
你觉得我和安吉拉应该去世界上哪个地方

1444
01:02:26.790 --> 01:02:27.750
in this world
来完成我们的双人旅行手记。

1445
01:02:27.750 --> 01:02:30.170
for our duo travel journal.
好啦。

1446
01:02:30.350 --> 01:02:30.750
Okay.
我们迫不及待想听到了。

1447
01:02:31.150 --> 01:02:32.510
We can't wait to hear.
我是真的很兴奋。

1448
01:02:32.690 --> 01:02:33.470
I really am excited.
谢谢你们大家的收听。

1449
01:02:33.770 --> 01:02:35.130
And thank you guys for listening.
我们希望你们喜欢我们的夏日旅行

1450
01:02:35.290 --> 01:02:37.210
We hope you enjoyed our summer travels
我们希望你们喜欢我们的夏日旅行

1451
01:02:37.210 --> 01:02:38.710
and we'll see you next time.
我们下期再见。

1452
01:02:38.830 --> 01:02:39.270
See you then.
到时见。

1453
01:02:39.750 --> 01:02:44.780
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

